{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/core.yaml && rg -n 'rvfi_valid|retirement|implementation_notes' CLAUDE.md .gitignore && rg --files cores/bench/test\"","aggregated_output":"name: bench\ndescription: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\n  freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\n  and operates only on this directory.\nisa: rv32im\nnret: 1\ntarget_fpga: tang-nano-20k\ntargets:\n  fmax_mhz: 135\n  lut4: 10000\n  coremark_iter_s: 300\n  coremark_per_mhz: 2.2\ncurrent:\n  fmax_mhz: 71.092\n  lut4: 3306\n  ff: 752\n  coremark_iter_s: 3.0e-06\n  coremark_per_mhz: 0.0\n  source_id: hyp-20261120-001-r6s0\n  updated: '2026-11-20T22:22:11.749243Z'\n.gitignore:87:cores/*/implementation_notes.md\nCLAUDE.md:11:| 1 | Top module `core` exposes an RVFI port set selected by `cores/<target>/core.yaml`'s `nret` field (default 2). **nret=1**: only `io_rvfi_*_0` ports exist; the single retirement always lands on channel 0. **nret=2**: both `io_rvfi_*_0` and `io_rvfi_*_1` exist; channel 0 carries the older of two simultaneous retirements, channel 1 the younger; single-retire cycles MUST place the retirement on channel 0 with `io_rvfi_valid_1 = 0`; all channel-1 ports MUST be driven (no X/Z, tie unused fields to `'0`). | cocotb smoke test, `riscv-formal` wrapper (`wrapper.sv` for nret=2, `wrapper_si.sv` for nret=1) |\nCLAUDE.md:14:| 4 | `rvfi_order` strictly monotonic +1 per retirement across both channels combined (no gaps, no duplicates). When both channels retire in the same cycle, channel-0 order = N and channel-1 order = N+1.                                       | `riscv-formal unique` check                  |\nCLAUDE.md:58:`cores/<TARGET>/test/test_*.py`. The agent's `implementation_notes.md`\nCLAUDE.md:59:lives at `cores/<TARGET>/implementation_notes.md` (gitignored). The\nCLAUDE.md:95:Cores declare their retirement width in `cores/<TARGET>/core.yaml`\nCLAUDE.md:111:  channel 1 (`io_rvfi_valid_1 = 0` plus all other `_1` fields driven\nCLAUDE.md:128:per-channel BMC checks assume `rvfi_valid_<ch>=1` to test their\nCLAUDE.md:130:hardwires `io_rvfi_valid_1 = 0`, that assumption becomes\ncores/bench/test/test_imm_gen.py\ncores/bench/test/conftest.py\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\ncores/bench/test/_helpers.py\ncores/bench/test/test_decoder.py\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv && rg -n 'div|mul|stall_ex_mem|mem_product|alu_result' cores/bench/rtl/{ex_stage,mem_stage,core,core_pkg,hazard_unit}.sv\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv && rg -n 'div|mul|stall_ex_mem|mem_product|alu_result' cores/bench/rtl/{ex_stage,mem_stage,core,core_pkg,hazard_unit}.sv\"", "aggregated_output": "// Integer results are available in EX. A multiply registers its operands\n// on issue and delivers its selected word in MEM. A blocking divide takes\n// over the same multiplier for seven clocks after its issue edge.\n`ifndef CORE_PKG_DEFINED\n`include \"core_pkg.sv\"\n`endif\nmodule alu (\n  input  logic        clock,\n  input  logic        reset,\n  input  logic [4:0]  op,\n  input  logic [31:0] a,\n  input  logic [31:0] b,\n  output logic [31:0] out,\n  input  logic        mul_issue,\n  output logic [31:0] mem_product,\n  input  logic        div_req_valid,\n  output logic        div_req_ready,\n  output logic        div_result_valid,\n  input  logic        div_result_ready,\n  output logic [31:0] div_result\n);\n\n  always_comb begin\n    case (op)\n      ALU_ADD:    out = a + b;\n      ALU_SUB:    out = a - b;\n      ALU_AND:    out = a & b;\n      ALU_OR:     out = a | b;\n      ALU_XOR:    out = a ^ b;\n      ALU_SLT:    out = {31'b0, $signed(a) < $signed(b)};\n      ALU_SLTU:   out = {31'b0, a < b};\n      ALU_SLL:    out = a << b[4:0];\n      ALU_SRL:    out = a >> b[4:0];\n      ALU_SRA:    out = $unsigned($signed(a) >>> b[4:0]);\n      ALU_LUI:    out = b;\n      default:    out = '0;\n    endcase\n  end\n\n  logic       busy_q;\n  logic [2:0] pass_q;\n  logic       div_issue;\n  assign div_req_ready = !busy_q && !div_result_valid;\n  assign div_issue = div_req_valid && div_req_ready;\n\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (reset) begin\n      busy_q           <= 1'b0;\n      pass_q           <= '0;\n      div_result_valid <= 1'b0;\n    end else if (div_issue) begin\n      busy_q <= 1'b1;\n      pass_q <= '0;\n    end else if (busy_q) begin\n      pass_q <= pass_q + 3'd1;\n      if (pass_q == 3'd6) begin\n        busy_q           <= 1'b0;\n        div_result_valid <= 1'b1;\n      end\n    end else if (div_result_ready) begin\n      div_result_valid <= 1'b0;\n    end\n  end\n\n`ifdef RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n  logic [31:0] alt_a_q, alt_b_q;\n  logic [4:0]  alt_op_q;\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (div_req_ready && (mul_issue || div_req_valid)) begin\n      \n…[8707 of 11779 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:37c5a74f29b2d5b5]…\nin.valid && !div_wait;\ncores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv:3:// Loads and multiplies produce data in MEM. An immediate consumer waits\ncores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv:7:// and divider waits hold the current ID/EX entry until EX can advance.\ncores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv:12:  input  logic       id_ex_mem_result,  // load or multiply in EX\ncores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv:17:  input  logic       div_wait,          // keep the issuing divide in ID/EX\ncores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv:30:  output logic       stall_ex_mem,      // EX/MEM register holds\ncores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv:38:  assign stall_ex_mem = !dmem_ready && ex_mem_mem_op;\ncores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv:39:  assign hold_mem_wb  = stall_ex_mem;\ncores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv:40:  assign stall_id     = stall_ex_mem || div_wait;\ncores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv:104:    logic [31:0] alu_result;\ncores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv:105:    logic        is_mul;         // select the registered operands' product in MEM\ncores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv:123:    logic [31:0] alu_result;\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
