{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_113","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":"# Registered Newton divide result\n\nPass 4 reuses the normalized-divisor register for the unsigned dividend shifted by `floor(log2(B))`. Pass 5 captures product bits 65 through 34 directly. Pass 6 uses the original dividend and divisor for the residual. Hardware and ALTOPS both take seven compute clocks.\n\nEX captures the corrected DIV/REM word alongside EX/MEM and holds it during a data-memory freeze. MEM masks and combines that word, the product, and the ordinary ALU or jump-link result into MEM/WB. Immediate DIV/REM consumers wait one cycle for WB forwarding. Independent successors advance on the divide transfer edge.\n\n## Implementation choices\n\n- DSP input A uses one-hot masks. Passes 1, 3, and 5 share a select because each reads the same staging register.\n- A 33-bit residual subtraction supplies both the comparison and the corrected remainder. Quotient correction and sign restoration share an incrementer because negating `Q + 1` gives `~Q`. A bit-vector equivalence check found the folded correction identical to the original for all input words and flags.\n- EX/MEM sets its divide selector on a valid divide response. The operand snapshots still capture at issue so RVFI reports the original forwarded values.\n\n## Measurements\n\n| Gowin placement | Fmax | Worst setup path |\n| --- | ---: | --- |\n| 0 | 74.125 MHz | WB select to data RAM |\n| 1 | 75.797 MHz | Fetch instruction RAM to PC |\n| 2 | 75.797 MHz | Fetch instruction RAM to PC |\n\nTen CRC-validated CoreMark iterations took **3,444,219 bracketed cycles** with both buses stalling. The median gives **220.07 iterations/s**, a 6.62% gain over 206.41. The measured median is 1.857 MHz below the scratch figure in the hypothesis. Placement 0 used 3,315 logic cells, 785 registers, seven BSRAMs, and two DSPs.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed in hardware and ALTOPS configurations.\n- All 103 cocotb tests passed, including 29 ALU and 30 pipeline tests. The MUL–DIV–MUL–DIV retirement gaps were 9, 2, and 10 clocks. An independent ADD followed DIV in one clock. A dependent store with two wait states retired four clocks after DIV and was accepted exactly once.\n- Selftest and all three random programs matched the retirement reference with zero-wait and stalled buses. CoreMark passed all five CRC checks and emitted the validation message.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
