{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg -c '<testcase ' cores/bench/test/*.result.xml; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"cores/bench/test/test_reg_file_runner.result.xml:5\ncores/bench/test/test_decoder_runner.result.xml:30\ncores/bench/test/test_alu_runner.result.xml:24\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline_runner.result.xml:13\ncores/bench/test/test_imm_gen_runner.result.xml:8\n# Fetch-stage agree predictor\n\nIF indexes 64 two-bit counters with PC[7:2]. Each entry starts at 01 on FPGA configuration and retains its training across core resets. A legal conditional branch uses the displacement sign XOR the counter's high bit. IF also predicts direct JAL. A predicted target must be word-aligned and below 0x00100000. Other fetches advance by four bytes.\n\nID/EX captures the selected direction and the counter snapshot with the instruction. A simultaneous EX update to the same index bypasses into that snapshot. This preserves the order of training for consecutive aliases and keeps the bypass off the fetch direction path.\n\nEX resolves transfers with forwarded operands. A direction mismatch on an advancing instruction flushes the younger instruction and corrects the PC, including during an instruction-bus stall. The same resolved successor drives RVFI. A taken misaligned transfer traps and falls through. Each advancing legal, nontrapping conditional branch trains once.\n\nThe target declares `nret: 1` in `core.yaml`. The implementation uses that interface. A guarded include in `core.sv` also supports the requested alphabetical Verilator source glob.\n\nThe pipeline tests check next-cycle fetch addresses, retirement PCs and successors, link writes, traps, and store enables. They exercise opposite-sign branches 256 bytes apart, a simultaneous read and write of their counter, loop exit behind a stalled store, instruction stalls, JAL, JALR, reserved branch encodings, misalignment, and targets outside both ends of instruction RAM.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
