{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_122","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git diff --name-only; du -sh \"$TMPDIR/registered-select\" \"$TMPDIR/verify/formal/riscv-formal/cores\"; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":"cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/forward_unit.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n33M\t/srv/hwebench/tmp/ec844b20/d44b7b79/registered-select\n469M\t/srv/hwebench/tmp/ec844b20/d44b7b79/verify/formal/riscv-formal/cores\n# Load-use latency prediction\n\nThe 64 one-bit predictors use load PC bits 7 through 2. Each starts fast and learns whether the last completed load at its index hit. EX probes a 1,024 × 78-bit synchronous RAM with the forwarded effective address. MEM verifies the RAM address, format, byte offset, alignment and validity while the consumer uses the saved formatted operand. A hit can retire with the data bus stalled.\n\nAn accepted RAM read installs the raw word and formatted result. An accepted word store installs an LW result. Byte and halfword stores invalidate their row. Reset sweeps all 1,024 rows while demand accesses continue. Same-row read/write collisions discard the probe, and MMIO always uses the bus. The predictor retains its timing history across a soft reset.\n\n## Implementation choice\n\nID compares both source fields against the two older destinations and registers the forwarding selectors. EX resolves misalignment and qualifies the destination write before ID captures those selectors. MEM uses the registered alignment decision for hit qualification, bus requests and RVFI masks. This moves the register comparisons off the consumer's EX path.\n\nOn a dependent miss, the consumer holds through the demand response. The response edge saves any outgoing WB operand the consumer also needs and moves the load to WB. The next cycle uses WB forwarding. Redirects, branch training and multiply/divide issue are suppressed until the operands are usable. An independent follower advances on the response edge.\n\n## Local verification\n\n| Check | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Verilator lint with `-Wall` | Passed without warnings |\n| Fast formal, target-configured single RVFI channel | 53 passed, 0 failed |\n| Cocotb pipeline suite | All 27 existing tests and four new directed tests passed |\n| Full-trace co-simulation | Selftest and three random programs matched the ISS with ready and stalled buses |\n| CoreMark, 10 iterations with both stall generators | 3,165,115 bracketed cycles, all five CRCs matched, validation message present |\n| Gowin placement options 0, 1 and 2 | 59.514, 63.231 and 63.231 MHz |\n| Median throughput | 199.77 iterations/s, 14.56% above the supplied 174.38 baseline |\n| Placement 0 resources | 3,542 logic cells, 822 registers, 14 BSRAMs and 2 DSPs |\n\nThe 20-cycle formal bound falls within the reset sweep. The directed tests run after the sweep and check warm forwarding with the bus stalled, a same-PC tag miss with a retained WB operand, stale branch/store/divide operands, subword formatting and RVFI data, store invalidation, RAM collisions, misaligned traps and MMIO exclusion.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
