{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_80","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/core.yaml | head -6 && rg -n 'RVFI|worktree|implementation_notes' CLAUDE.md | head -12\"","aggregated_output":"name: bench\ndescription: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\n  freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\n  and operates only on this directory.\nisa: rv32im\nnret: 1\n11:| 1 | Top module `core` exposes an RVFI port set selected by `cores/<target>/core.yaml`'s `nret` field (default 2). **nret=1**: only `io_rvfi_*_0` ports exist; the single retirement always lands on channel 0. **nret=2**: both `io_rvfi_*_0` and `io_rvfi_*_1` exist; channel 0 carries the older of two simultaneous retirements, channel 1 the younger; single-retire cycles MUST place the retirement on channel 0 with `io_rvfi_valid_1 = 0`; all channel-1 ports MUST be driven (no X/Z, tie unused fields to `'0`). | cocotb smoke test, `riscv-formal` wrapper (`wrapper.sv` for nret=2, `wrapper_si.sv` for nret=1) |\n29:- `tools/` — orchestrator, worktree manager, eval gates.\n48:worktree's `git status` must only show allowed paths; the main checkout's\n52:worktree is deleted before the build, so the eval only consumes artifacts\n58:`cores/<TARGET>/test/test_*.py`. The agent's `implementation_notes.md`\n59:lives at `cores/<TARGET>/implementation_notes.md` (gitignored). The\n64:named `core` whose IO matches the RVFI wrapper's expectations: the\n67:`io_dmemREn`, `io_dmemReady`), `clock`, `reset`, and the RVFI port\n81:- Change `core`'s top-level IO shape relative to the `nret` value declared in `core.yaml` — specifically: the imem/dmem port set, and the RVFI port set (only `_0` fields for `nret: 1`; both `_0` and `_1` for `nret: 2` with channel-0-older convention and the single-retire-on-channel-0 rule).\n93:### RVFI contract: nret=1 vs nret=2\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
