{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_141","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git diff -- cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py && cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":"diff --git a/cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py b/cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\nindex d0b0b91..4f6b0c3 100644\n--- a/cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n+++ b/cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n@@ -609,6 +609,32 @@ async def buffered_read_skipped_by_store(dut):\n     assert rets[7][\"cycle\"] == rets[6][\"cycle\"] + 2\n \n \n+@cocotb.test()\n+async def buffered_wb_forward_across_demand_wait(dut):\n+    # The LH hits a warmed row. The following cold LW holds the ADD in EX\n+    # for three cycles after the LH retires, with both inputs selecting WB.\n+    program = [\n+        LW(0, 0, 64), NOP(), _i(66, 0, 1, 1, 3), LW(2, 0, 68),\n+        ADD(3, 1, 1), ADD(4, 2, 3), EBREAK(),\n+    ]\n+    reads = []\n+\n+    def ready(ren, wen, addr, wdata):\n+        if ren:\n+            reads.append(addr)\n+        return addr != 68 or reads.count(68) == 4\n+\n+    rets, _ = await _run(dut, program, {64: 0x80F17EA5, 68: 7},\n+                         dmem_ready=ready, sweep_cycles=1025)\n+    _check_linear_retirements(rets, program)\n+    assert reads == [64, 68, 68, 68, 68]\n+    hit, miss, add, mixed = rets[2:6]\n+    assert (hit[\"mem_rmask\"], hit[\"mem_rdata\"], hit[\"rd_wdata\"]) == (12, 0x80F17EA5, 0xFFFF80F1)\n+    assert miss[\"cycle\"] == hit[\"cycle\"] + 4\n+    assert (add[\"rs1_rdata\"], add[\"rs2_rdata\"], add[\"rd_wdata\"]) == (0xFFFF80F1, 0xFFFF80F1, 0xFFFF01E2)\n+    assert (mixed[\"rs1_rdata\"], mixed[\"rs2_rdata\"], mixed[\"rd_wdata\"]) == (7, 0xFFFF01E2, 0xFFFF01E9)\n+\n+\n @cocotb.test()\n async def buffered_reset_sweep(dut):\n     # Warm the last two rows, then reset against different backing data.\n# Split load writeback\n\nMEM formats the resolved row and the bus word independently. On each MEM/WB advance it captures the formatted row, the normal result, and the verified row-select bit. During a data-bus wait the data and select hold while WB valid clears. The registered bit selects the register-file write and RVFI destination value. It also selects the corresponding raw word for RVFI memory read data.\n\nDecode splits each winning MEM forwarding match using the same row decision. Both operands can independently select the normal WB word, buffered WB word, EX/MEM result, or product. A held consumer retains its selects. A pipeline regression exercises both operands forwarding a signed halfword from the buffer while a younger demand load stalls for three cycles.\n\nTwo refinements address the wider EX operand network. ID captures the ALU's immediate or masked register-file contribution alongside the raw operands. EX combines that contribution with the two forwarding pairs and uses the existing branch-target adder for AUIPC. The load formatter folds width into its lane selects so the row and bus paths share control logic.\n\n## Local results\n\n| Measurement | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Verilator lint | Passed without warnings |\n| Cocotb | All five suites passed, including the held-consumer regression |\n| Retirement trace co-simulation | Selftest and three random programs passed with and without stalls |\n| Stalled CoreMark | 10 iterations in 3,081,605 bracketed cycles, from 11,835 to 3,093,440 |\n| CoreMark validation | CRCs matched `e9f5`, `e714`, `1fd7`, `8e3a`, and `fcaf`. UART reported “Correct operation validated.” |\n| Gowin Fmax, placement options 0 / 1 / 2 | 80.891 / 86.589 / 86.589 MHz |\n| Median Fmax | 86.589 MHz |\n\nThe initial two-register split measured 81.535 MHz median. With the refinements, the median placement's longest reported path runs from the fetch reset register to the fall-through PC register in 16.843 ns. Placement 0 still has a critical path from the registered row forwarding select to the EX/MEM ALU result. Timing remains below the 91.61 MHz promotion threshold.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
