{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat Makefile; ls -l formal; ls -la cores/bench; ls /opt/gowin; printenv | rg '\"'^(GOWIN|RISCV|HW|FORMAL|TARGET|COCOTB|PYTHON|TMPDIR|EVAL)'\"'\"", "aggregated_output": ".PHONY: help lint test test-infra cosim formal fpga timing next loop report bench clean\n.DEFAULT_GOAL := help\n\n# Resolve OSS CAD Suite path so commands work even when the user hasn't\n# sourced .toolchain/oss-cad-suite/environment in this shell.\nTOOLCHAIN_DIR := $(CURDIR)/.toolchain\nOSS_BIN       := $(TOOLCHAIN_DIR)/oss-cad-suite/bin\nLOCAL_BIN     := $(TOOLCHAIN_DIR)/bin\nexport PATH := $(OSS_BIN):$(LOCAL_BIN):$(PATH)\n\n# Orchestrator knobs (pass-through to tools.orchestrator):\n#   N        — number of rounds for `make loop` (default 10).\n#   K        — tournament size, slots per round (default 1 = sequential).\n#   AGENT    — codex (default) or claude. Honors a pre-existing\n#              AGENT_PROVIDER env var if AGENT isn't set on the make\n#              command line.\n#   BASE     — when forking a new TARGET, copy from cores/<BASE>/.\n#              Default: baseline (orchestrator-side default).\n#   COREMARK — target CoreMark iterations/sec (e.g. '370').\n#   LUT      — target LUT count (e.g. '3000').\n#   WORKTREE — default ON. `make loop` first creates a dedicated git worktree\n#              at .worktrees/<TARGET>/ on branch core-<TARGET> and re-execs\n#              itself there. Lets two `make loop` invocations for different\n#              TARGETs run in parallel without git index/merge collisions.\n#              To opt out (run directly on the current branch + cwd) pass\n#              an explicit empty value: `make loop TARGET=v1 WORKTREE=`.\nN        ?= 10\nK        ?= 1\nAGENT    ?= $(or $(AGENT_PROVIDER),codex)\nBASE     ?=\nCOREMARK ?=\nLUT      ?=\nWORKTREE ?= 1\n\n# Compose optional CLI flags for the orchestrator. Empty vars produce\n# empty strings so the orchestrator falls back to its defaults.\nORCH_FLAGS  = --iterations $(N) --tournament-size $(K)\nifneq ($(strip $(BASE)),)\n  ORCH_FLAGS += --base $(BASE)\nendif\nifneq ($(strip $(COREMARK)),)\n  ORCH_FLAGS += --coremark-target $(COREMARK)\nendif\nifneq ($(strip $(LUT)),)\n  ORCH_FLAGS += --lut-target $(LUT)\nendif\n\n# Multi-core: TARGET selects the core under cores/<TARGET>\n…[6127 of 9199 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:cd1f40866686f2aa]…\nwxrwx---+ 5 nobody nogroup  4096 Nov 21 09:07 .\ndrwxrwx---+ 3 nobody nogroup  4096 Nov 21 09:07 ..\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup     0 Nov 21 09:07 CORE_PHILOSOPHY.md\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup 11710 Nov 21 09:07 LESSONS.md\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup   545 Nov 21 09:07 core.yaml\ndrwxrwx---+ 2 nobody nogroup  4096 Nov 21 09:07 experiments\ndrwxrwx---+ 2 nobody nogroup  4096 Nov 21 09:07 rtl\ndrwxrwx---+ 2 nobody nogroup  4096 Nov 21 09:07 test\nIDE\nProgrammer\ndeps\ngowin.tgz.sha256\nHWE_AGENT_TMP=/srv/hwebench/tmp/ec844b20\nGOWIN_HOME=/opt/gowin\nHWE_AGENT_PATH=/srv/hwebench/cli/codex-0.170.0:/srv/hwebench/bin:/srv/hwebench/venv/bin:/srv/hwebench/local/bin:/srv/hwebench/toolchain/oss-cad-suite/bin:/srv/hwebench/toolchain/bin:/srv/hwebench/venv/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin\nHWE_AGENT_PYTHONUSERBASE=/srv/hwebench/local\nTMPDIR=/srv/hwebench/tmp/ec844b20/58c8098c\nPYTHONUSERBASE=/srv/hwebench/local\nHWE_AGENT_USER=hwebench\nHWE_AGENT_HOME=/srv/hwebench/homes/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep3\nTARGET=bench\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
