{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_133","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git status --short; git diff --check; wc -l cores/bench/rtl/load_tag_plane.sv cores/bench/implementation_notes.md; sed -n '1,5p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n?? cores/bench/rtl/load_tag_plane.sv\n  56 cores/bench/rtl/load_tag_plane.sv\n  16 cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\n  72 total\n# Resolved load tag comparison\n\nGowin reached a median **89.475 MHz**, up 2.16% from 87.580 MHz and below the 91.61 MHz promotion threshold. The ten CoreMark iterations took 3,081,605 bracketed cycles and scored 290.35 iterations per second. Placement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 84.887, 89.475 and 89.475 MHz respectively.\n\nEach accepted RAM fill or full-word store replaces two 16-bit masks at the resolved row index. Partial stores and the reset sweep clear both masks. EX probes each plane with the ten-bit row index and the corresponding four tag bits. Both match bits advance with the raw word. MEM qualifies their conjunction with the registered range, alignment, sweep and same-row collision checks. The early port retains its binary tag and validity bit.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
