{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_111","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":"# RV32M linear reciprocal divider\n\nThe vendor FPGA evaluation measured **244.23 CoreMark iterations/s**. Ten CRC-validated iterations took **3,097,817 cycles** between the MMIO markers with both bus stalls enabled. The **75.658 MHz** median cleared the 74.887 MHz threshold by 0.771 MHz.\n\n## Implementation\n\nIn `rtl/alu.sv`, a synchronous 1,024 × 48-bit ROM supplies a tangent intercept and slope. Unsigned 64-bit elaboration arithmetic rounds the intercept down and the slope up. The divider shifts the dividend with two guard bits during the lookup, registers the slope product, and rounds its contribution upward before subtracting it from the intercept. The high 32 bits of the 66-bit quotient product give the estimate.\n\nThe input magnitudes stay stable through the response. This lets intermediate registers run without individual pass enables. Pass 4 captures the quotient. Pass 5 computes both candidate remainders and registers `Q+1` in parallel. Moving the increment here shortens the work after the correction decision. Pass 6 uses the subtraction borrow to select the magnitude and registers the sign-corrected result. The request controller holds that result through backpressure.\n\nOrdinary multiplies have dedicated signed 33-bit input registers and deliver the selected word in MEM on consecutive issues. The ALTOPS branch uses the same issue and response timing.\n\n## Timing and area\n\n| Gowin placement | Fmax |\n| --- | ---: |\n| 0 | 70.890 MHz |\n| 1 | 75.658 MHz |\n| 2 | 75.658 MHz |\n\nPlacement 0 used 3,444 logic cells, 877 registers, 15 BSRAMs and seven DSPs. The median placement's worst path ran from the MEM/WB ALU result through forwarding to the saved-instruction memory in fetch. Placement 0 fell below the frequency threshold.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Verilator passed the requested full-core lint command with zero warnings.\n- Local formal passed on the first run of the final RTL. All 53 fast ALTOPS checks passed with the single-retirement wrapper.\n- All 110 cocotb cases passed. The unsigned boundary test checked 67,288 DIVU and REMU transactions across 8,418 divisors against Python `divmod`. Signed tests exercised overflow, zero divisors, both signs near exact multiples, and a held remainder during consecutive MUL issues.\n- Selftest and three random programs matched the retirement reference with zero-wait and stalled buses. CoreMark matched all five canonical CRCs and emitted `Correct operation validated.`\n- A separate exact-rational check bounded the pre-floor quotient underestimate for every reachable table row at each exponent. For exponents above ten the bound was below 0.831446 quotient units. The overall bound was `(2^32-1)/2^32` at divisor one.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
