{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_163","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'tail -n 4 \"$TMPDIR/predictor-checks/cores/bench/generated/timing/gowin_p0/gw.log\"; date -u; ls -lt \"$TMPDIR/predictor-checks/formal/\"last_run* | head -n 2; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":"Generate file \"/srv/hwebench/tmp/ec844b20/8881c7b5/predictor-checks/cores/bench/generated/timing/gowin_p0/impl/pnr/core_bench.tr.html\" completed\nGenerate file \"/srv/hwebench/tmp/ec844b20/8881c7b5/predictor-checks/cores/bench/generated/timing/gowin_p0/impl/pnr/core_bench.tr\" completed\nSat Nov 21 03:46:50 2026\n\nSat Nov 21 02:46:51 UTC 2026\n-rw-rw----+ 1 hwebench hwebench 298398 Nov 21 03:43 /srv/hwebench/tmp/ec844b20/8881c7b5/predictor-checks/formal/last_run-wksV8qVPa.log\n-rw-rw----+ 1 hwebench hwebench 324104 Nov 21 03:38 /srv/hwebench/tmp/ec844b20/8881c7b5/predictor-checks/formal/last_run-waqPc8hUE.log\n# Two-bank load predictor\n\nID probes two 512-word banks using the existing pointer sources and a 12-bit base hint. Each bank computes its upper row bits independently of the carry out of bit 5. EX selects the registered response and compares its expected base against all four physical rs1 sources. A certified hit permits the immediate consumer to advance. MEM still probes the exact effective address and supplies the architectural load value.\n\nThe collision check uses the selected row's tag to distinguish a same-index older load hit from a fill. Both read ports sampled the same row on the same edge whenever the early response is available and the indices coincide. This keeps the resolved MEM hit signal out of the early interlock. Stores, including a store released after a hold, veto a same-index bypass.\n\nThe hot 68 + 4 load retires immediately before its consumer. The cold access incurs one dependency bubble. Pipeline tests also check bank and page carries, same-low-12-bit pointer aliases, subword lanes, and overlapping reads, fills and held stores. A SAT check of the RTL address equations covered all 16,777,216 base-low and displacement pairs.\n\nVerilator lint and all 117 cocotb cases passed. Co-simulation matched the ISS for selftest and three random programs with and without bus stalls. Ten CoreMark iterations with both buses stalling took 3,057,579 cycles between the MMIO markers, 4,954 fewer than the baseline. All five CRCs matched and the UART reported “Correct operation validated.”\n\nThe final RTL passed all 53 checks in the single-retire formal suite. An intermediate version failed during Yosys elaboration on a variable-indexed struct field. Using packed memory words and accessing named fields on each bank's registered response fixed elaboration. There was no SMT counterexample.\n\nGowin placement options 0, 1 and 2 measured 72.695, 75.438 and 75.438 MHz. The 75.438 MHz median gives 246.72 CoreMark iterations per second, below the 82.815 MHz promotion threshold for this cycle count. On the median placement, the longest setup path ran from the saved instruction to the fetch PC. The path from the saved instruction to the early bank read was second.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
