{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'train_count|u_if\\\\.|train_(en|index|value)' cores/bench/test; cat formal/checks_si.cfg\"","aggregated_output":"[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\n# the full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\n# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nalways @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n\n[verilog-files]\n# run_all.sh rebuilds this section from the actual rtl/ glob; the list\n# below is overwritten before genchecks runs. Kept as a placeholder so\n# the section is syntactically present for any reader inspecting the cfg.\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/core.sv\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_12", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat Makefile | sed -n '68,160p'; ls -la formal; ls cores/bench/test; ls /opt/gowin\"", "aggregated_output": "  # WORKTREE-mode paths (only consumed when WORKTREE= is set on `make loop`).\n  WT_BRANCH  := core-$(TARGET)\n  WT_PATH    := $(CURDIR)/.worktrees/$(TARGET)\nendif\n\nexport RTL_DIR CORE_NAME OBJ_DIR GEN_DIR\n\nhelp:\n\t@echo \"Targets (most accept TARGET=<core_name>):\"\n\t@echo \"  make lint TARGET=v1     — verilator lint over cores/<TARGET>/rtl/*.sv\"\n\t@echo \"  make test TARGET=v1     — cocotb unit tests under cores/<TARGET>/test/\"\n\t@echo \"  make cosim TARGET=v1    — RVFI cosim against Python ISS\"\n\t@echo \"  make formal TARGET=v1   — riscv-formal fast suite (with ALTOPS)\"\n\t@echo \"  make formal-deep TARGET=v1 — full formal suite without ALTOPS (slow, bitvector-correct)\"\n\t@echo \"  make fpga TARGET=v1     — FPGA fitness eval (Gowin Fmax + CoreMark cycles)\"\n\t@echo \"  make timing TARGET=v1   — Gowin Fmax and worst paths (placement option 0)\"\n\t@echo \"  make bench              — build selftest + coremark ELFs\"\n\t@echo \"  make next TARGET=v1     — one orchestrator round\"\n\t@echo \"  make loop TARGET=v1 N=10 — N orchestrator rounds (auto-spawns .worktrees/<TARGET> on branch core-<TARGET>; pass WORKTREE= to opt out)\"\n\t@echo \"  make report TARGET=v1   — per-core experiment summary\"\n\t@echo \"  make clean TARGET=v1    — remove per-core build artifacts (use with TARGET=)\"\n\t@echo \"  make test-infra         — run orchestrator infra tests under tools/\"\n\t@echo \"\"\n\t@echo \"Available cores:\"\n\t@for d in cores/*/; do echo \"  - $$(basename $$d)\"; done 2>/dev/null || echo \"  (none yet)\"\n\n# verilator lint over $(RTL_DIR)/.\n# -Wno-MULTITOP: until phase 2's core.sv lands and instantiates everything,\n# rtl/ legitimately has multiple top modules. Drop this once phase 2 is in.\nlint:\n\t@if ls $(RTL_DIR)/*.sv >/dev/nul