{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_156","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg --files --hidden --no-ignore tools -g '*.pyc' | head -40; git diff --numstat; git status --short; sed -n '1,160p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"tools/__pycache__/__init__.cpython-313.pyc\ntools/eval/__pycache__/gowin.cpython-313.pyc\ntools/eval/__pycache__/fpga.cpython-313.pyc\ntools/eval/__pycache__/__init__.cpython-313.pyc\ntools/eval/__pycache__/_subprocess.cpython-313.pyc\ntools/eval/__pycache__/formal.cpython-313.pyc\n71\t56\tcores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\n57\t6\tcores/bench/test/test_alu.py\n M cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_alu.py\n# Piecewise-linear reciprocal divider\n\nThe divider uses a 512-row, 36-bit coefficient ROM, an 11×16 interpolation product and one downward-rounded Newton refinement. RV32M multiplies and the four wide divide products share the same registered 36×36 multiplier. Division samples its operands on issue, presents a result seven clocks later and holds it until transfer. Independent multiplies can issue on adjacent clocks.\n\n## Implementation details\n\n- The ROM initializes both coefficients with unsigned 64-bit arithmetic. The magnitude registers hold the division inputs, allowing normalization, coefficient lookup and dividend scaling to use continuously clocked intermediate registers.\n- For nonzero divisors only the low 18 bits of the Newton factor E vary. Checking both ends of every constant-P interval gave an exact range of 3 through 110,487 for E − 2³⁴.\n- The last edge forms both T = A − Q×B and T − B using a precomputed 33-bit A − B. The sign of T − B selects the correction. Quotient increment and sign restoration share one final adder.\n- The selected RTL change is confined to the ALU. A separate fetch and load-address timing experiment reached 76.037 MHz with 3,684 logic cells. The ALU-only implementation meets the stated threshold with 3,625 logic cells.\n\n## Arithmetic checks\n\nThe cocotb tests compare all four divide and remainder instructions with exact integer results at bin boundaries and around divisor multiples. They also check the registered refined reciprocal, discarded dividend bits, sign handling, zero divisors, signed overflow, result backpressure and adjacent multiply issues. For 0xffffffff divided by 7 the RTL produced a trial residual of 10 and a corrected remainder of 3.\n\nAn independent integer sweep checked 0 ≤ 2⁶⁵ − N×R < 4×N for all 2³¹ normalized divisors. The largest reciprocal underestimate was 0.654881 × 2⁻³² at N = 0x82801000.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
