{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-001-r1s0.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261120-001-r1s0\ntitle: \"Resolve two quotient bits per combinational divider stage\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The baseline runs at a median 5.442 MHz. Its reported 199.837 ns path traverses\n  operand forwarding and the EX ALU. The signed and unsigned division and remainder\n  operators in alu.sv are the strongest candidates for that depth. A shorter\n  combinational divider could raise Fmax even on cycles executing an ordinary ADD.\nhypothesis: |\n  Implement DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU with one unrolled radix-4 magnitude divider\n  in the existing EX cycle. Each of 16 stages consumes the next two dividend bits\n  and produces two quotient bits. For trial remainder T = 4*R + next_pair,\n  form T-D, T-2D and T-3D in parallel. Use their borrow bits to select the\n  largest fitting multiple and its already-computed difference, passing T through\n  for digit zero. This halves the number of dependent digit decisions relative\n  to a binary restoring divider. The tradeoff is routing three candidates into\n  each remainder mux. With the same instruction latencies and stall sequence,\n  the bracketed cycle count should stay at 4,491,485. A median above 5.70 MHz\n  at that count would clear the tournament threshold.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 25\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      In the real-arithmetic branch, convert signed operands to unsigned magnitudes\n      and precompute D, 2D and 3D once with 34-bit precision. Stage i (1 through 16)\n      needs only 2*i trial bits because it has consumed that many dividend bits.\n      Flag any multiple with bits above that width as too large, then use a\n      zero-extended subtraction for each low-width difference and borrow. Assemble\n      the quotient from the selected digits and use the final remainder directly.\n      For signed operations, negate the quotient when operand signs differ and\n      give the remainder the dividend's sign. Handle zero divisor before output\n      sign correction (all-ones quotient, original dividend as remainder) and\n      preserve INT_MIN/-1 results (INT_MIN, zero). Retain the existing ALTOPS\n      expressions and combinational ALU interface.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
