{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-003-r1s2.yaml | head -50'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261120-003-r1s2\ntitle: Predict direct branches with a 64-entry agree predictor at fetch\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The baseline fetches PC+4 until EX resolves a transfer. Since IF feeds ID\n  combinationally, a taken branch or jump discards one younger fetch slot.\n  A reference trace between the CoreMark markers contains 529,588 conditional\n  branches, of which 294,425 change the successor, plus 49,367 direct jumps.\n  The baseline's 199.837 ns worst path crosses forwarding and the EX ALU.\n  Predicting these direct transfers in IF can save cycles with a small table.\nhypothesis: |\n  Index 64 two-bit saturating counters with fetch PC[7:2]. Use the offset\n  sign as the default direction for a legal conditional branch (backward\n  taken, forward fall-through). Predict taken = offset_sign XOR counter[1].\n  The counter learns whether to invert the default, so a hot backedge and\n  a usually untaken forward guard can share an entry constructively. Predict\n  direct JAL taken. Compute the signed B/J target in parallel with the table\n  lookup and select it only for a word-aligned address in instruction RAM.\n  Use PC+4 for every other fetch, including JALR. Carry the selected direction\n  bit with the accepted instruction. Direct targets are exact by construction,\n  so EX can detect a miss by comparing this bit with the resolved direction.\n  A miss redirects to the resolved next PC and kills the younger instruction.\n  Correct predictions let the successor enter ID/EX immediately. An isolated\n  RTL prototype completed ten 2K CoreMark iterations in 4,194,484 bracketed\n  cycles with both bus stalls enabled, versus 4,491,485 on the baseline.\n  All five CRCs matched. Gowin reported 5.214, 5.486 and 5.486 MHz across\n  the three placement options. The median gives 13.08 iter/s, a 7.9% gain\n  over 12.12. The prototype used 12 LUT-RAM primitives versus 8 at baseline.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Initialize counters to 01 (weak agreement) at configuration. Use one\n      asynchronous read indexed by the fetch PC and one synchronous write.\n      Decode legal B and JAL from raw imem_data. Calculate the signed target\n      and feed the guarded prediction into the PC mux. Give reset first\n      priority, then an EX correction even if imem is stalled, then the\n      prediction on an accepted fetch. Hold the PC on other stalls.\n      Train from the resolving branch's\n      saved counter. Increment on disagreement with the offset sign, decrement\n      on agreement, and saturate at either end. When an older branch updates\n      the index being fetched, bypass the new count into the younger branch's\n      training snapshot. Record the direction actually selected for fetch.\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Add predicted_taken and the two-bit counter snapshot to both IF/ID and ID/EX.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: Latch the direction and counter snapshot with the instruction using its hold and bubble controls.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20261120-002-r1s1.last'","aggregated_output":"Wrote and schema-validated the [structural hypothesis](./cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-002-r1s1.yaml). It proposes a shared four-pass divider to shorten the 199.837 ns path through EX.\n\nThe canonical CoreMark binary executes no divide or remainder instructions between its timing markers, so the added latency should have little effect on measured cycles. At the baseline cycle count, raising median Fmax from 5.442 to 8.163 MHz would deliver the projected **50% fitness gain**. FPGA timing remains unmeasured.","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
