  the acceptance margin. The main risks are routing the parallel comparisons\n  and the independent saved-instruction path to the PC. The parallel-pair\n  design has yet to be timed.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      At ID/EX capture the pair classification fr\n…[1054 of 4126 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:8ae27e11e759a6b6]…\nr reversed pairs derive the opposite strict order from equality\n      and less-than. For example, WB less than product is true exactly\n      when product less than WB and product equal to WB are both false.\n      Mask and combine the one-bit results with the saved pair selects.\n      Apply funct3 polarity for BEQ/BNE, BLT/BGE and\n      BLTU/BGEU. Use the selected condition for redirect, training and\n      architectural next PC, retaining the alignment check and misaligned\n      taken-branch trap. Continue to use forwarded words for RVFI.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Exercise both orientations of WB versus ordinary and product bypass,\n      two operands from the same writer, x0, and RF versus each bypass.\n      Include signed and unsigned operands that first differ in each byte,\n      equality at the signed boundary, a branch held by dmem backpressure\n      and a misaligned target. Check branch direction, fetch recovery,\n      retirement order and suppression of a wrong-path store.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
