{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nlines=Path('.tmp/agent-logs/impl.hyp-20261121-001-r11s0.log').read_text().splitlines()\nfor line in lines:\n try: evt=json.loads(line)\n except ValueError: continue\n item=evt.get('item',{})\n if item.get('type')=='agent_message': print(item.get('text','')[:1300])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"I’ll check the worktree layout and verification commands, then implement the lookahead in IF and the direct recovery path in EX.\nThe existing pipeline suite and co-simulation pass with the lookahead enabled. I’m adding directed tests for sustained bus-low issue, recovery after a wrong probe, and a queued write that overwrites a probe during a divide hold.\nThe new directed tests pass, including consecutive retirements with the instruction bus held low. The timing reports exposed a long path from EX into fetch-state enables, so I’m testing a version that registers the admission decision separately from the probe data.\nThe selected RTL passed all 53 formal checks, all 115 cocotb cases, and co-simulation. Its measured median was 81.435 MHz over 3,078,099 bracketed cycles, which improves throughput by 2.17% and falls short of the promotion threshold.\nImplemented and verified the registered successor-RAM lookahead. Strict lint, all 53 formal checks, all 115 cocotb cases, and co-simulation passed.\n\nCoreMark completed 10 iterations in **3,078,099 bracketed cycles** with all five CRCs correct. Median Fmax was **81.435 MHz**, yielding **264.56 iterations/s**—a **2.17% gain** over the champion, below the promotion threshold.\n\n[Implementation notes](cores/bench/implementation_notes.md)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
