{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-002-r9s1.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261121-002-r9s1\ntitle: Select physical writeback banks when decode issues each consumer\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion runs ten iterations in 3,097,817 cycles. Repeating Gowin\n  placement 1 reproduced its 76.071 MHz median. The first setup path runs\n  from the reciprocal seed ROM through the shared DSP to MEM/WB write_data\n  in 18.440 ns. The next path starts at the registered rs1 forwarding\n  select and reaches the fetch PC in 18.438 ns. The first crosses a result\n  mux after multiplication. The second crosses a priority mux before EX\n  address generation and load-use control. Both boundaries depend on the\n  same information about which older instruction supplies an operand.\nhypothesis: |\n  Put the MEM/WB register boundary directly on the DSP output. Capture\n  product[31:0] and product[63:32] in separate word banks alongside the\n  ordinary result. In ID, assign each source to its next EX input using the\n  youngest matching writer, its pipeline stage and its decoded operation.\n  The five possible inputs are the captured RF word, EX/MEM bypass, ordinary\n  WB word, low product and high product. Record the one-hot choice with the\n  operand. EX can mask and combine these physical words in parallel. Decode\n  the PC and immediate substitutions at the same issue boundary so the\n  arithmetic inputs each have a single selection network. The register file\n  and RVFI use a separate architectural WB mux.\n\n  This preserves one multiply issue per clock, the verified early-load\n  bypass and existing dependency bubbles. A gain must come from a shorter\n  clock period. At the champion's cycle count the acceptance threshold is\n  79.57 MHz. The main risk is routing five wide sources to each operand.\n\n  A precursor with a single selected-product bank retained all five CRCs\n  and 3,097,817 cycles. It reached 64.507 MHz median with fetch as the\n  limiting path. The separate raw product banks still\n  require placement and timing.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rt\n…[1416 of 4488 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:52da25682468434a]…\nhots.\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Carry the raw and arithmetic operand selects in the ID/EX bundle.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Wire the producer class and all three result banks to their consumers.\n      Advance source metadata on exactly the existing operand capture edge\n      and hold it through divide and memory stalls.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Route the two raw product halves from the ALU to MEM. Use the\n      registered enables to AND-mask and OR the physical sources at\n      each operand port. Feed rs1 directly to the existing address adder and\n      use the arithmetic-port enables for PC and immediate substitutions.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Alternate low-product, high-product and integer writers to one rd,\n      then issue a consumer using different banks on rs1 and rs2\n      across a data wait. Check the forwarded operands, exact result,\n      single accepted store and consecutive channel-0 retirement orders.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
