ds:    n/a (governs validity of subsequent retirements).\nmodule hazard_unit (\n  input  logic       id_ex_mem_result,  // result unavailable for EX bypass\n  input  logic [4:0] id_ex_rd,          // ID/EX.rd\n  input  logic [4:0] if_id_rs1,         // IF/ID instr[19:15]  (next rs1)\n  input  logic [4:0] if_id_rs2,         // IF/ID instr[24:20]  (next rs2)\n  input  logic       redirect,          // EX has resolved a branch/jump\n  input\nitem_33 total 28\ndrwxrwx---+ 2 hwebench hwebench 4096 Nov 21 01:20 .\ndrwxrwx---+ 4 hwebench hwebench 4096 Nov 21 01:20 ..\n-rw-rw----+ 1 hwebench hwebench  797 Nov 21 01:20 cmd.do\n-rw-rw----+ 1 hwebench hwebench  728 Nov 21 01:20 core_bench.log\n-rw-rw----+ 1 hweben\n…[6327 of 9399 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:337311c8d2553723]…\ne operation-specific surrogate in ALTOPS mode.\n\nThe directed regression alternates writers to x5, checks simultaneous EX/MEM and low-product forwarding, and holds a high-product consumer behind a store for three wait cycles. It checks both source values, the result, the single store handshake and every channel-0 retirement order.\n\nDecode also classifies the producer itself when it issues. That one-hot class travels through EX/MEM into WB. ID captures a local arithmetic word for each port, substituting PC or immediate into the RF slot when appropriate. This keeps each arithmet\nImplemented decode-time writeback bank selection. Lint, all 53 formal checks, cocotb, and cosimulation passed. CoreMark retained all five CRCs and completed ten iterations in 3,097,817 cycles.\n\nThe submitted RTL reached **74.789 MHz** on Gowin placement 1, below the **79.57 MHz** target. A faster variant reached a 76.895 MHz median, but its final formal check was still running. [Implementation notes](cores/bench/implementation_notes.md)\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
