 control selects the issued prediction, the held fetch address or the EX correction. Successor reads and pair training still require admission. EX uses the saved JALR forecast address directly for its independent target check.\n\nThe pipeline carries the selected direct direction and training count. EX reconstructs the other direct address from the issuing PC and immediate. To shorten the admission path, ID also evaluates the direct miss decision for both possible comparator outcomes. EX selects the appropriate bit after comparing the forwarded operands. The early load-buffer hit check verifies the carries implied by the expected word address in parallel. These two changes preserve branch training and load bypass behavior.\n\nThe new pipeline tests check cold fetches across both sides of a 2 KiB boundary, the first and last RAM words, a misaligned jump, and replacement of a saved JAL by a ready-bus backward branch. They check the first target fetch on saved-word hits with poisoned bus data, RVFI order, link values and store side effects. The correction test holds both the wrong-path fetch and the recovery address through instruction waits.\n\n## Local results\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Verilator lint | Passed with no warnings |\n| Cocotb | All five test suites passed, including 40 pipeline cases |\n| Formal | 53 passed, 0 failed on the first run for this RTL |\n| Co-simulation | All five ELFs passed, including the stalled and zero-wait RVFI comparisons |\n| Stalled CoreMark | 3,062,533 bracketed cycles, all five canonical CRCs, validated UART output, zero out-of-bounds accesses |\n| Gowin placement options 0, 1, 2 | 76.702, 80.074, 80.074 MHz |\n\nMedian Fmax was 80.074 MHz, below the 82.9491 MHz acceptance threshold at this cycle count. The worst option-1 setup path runs from EX operand forwarding through address calculation to the successor RAM write enable.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
