{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -n 1 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20261121-002-r13s1\", \"title\": \"Let a posted RAM store drain while MEM services cache hits\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"An unaccepted store currently freezes every pipeline stage behind MEM,\\nincluding independent integer instructions and loads whose full word is\\nalready resident. Ten CoreMark iterations take 3,081,605 bracketed cycles.\\nRegistering a fallback lookup for unverified loads added 99,982 cycles in\\na scratch run. Ordinary stores offer a way to overlap a bus wait without\\ncharging each uncertain load an extra clock.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"An unaccepted store currently freezes every pipeline stage behind MEM,\\nincluding independent integer instructions and loads whose full word is\\nalready resident. Ten CoreMark iterations take 3,081,605 bracketed cycles.\\nRegistering a fallback lookup for unverified loads added 99,982 cycles in\\na scratch run. Ordinary stores offer a way to overlap a bus wait without\\ncharging each uncertain load an extra clock.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Split the external write port from MEM with one posted-store entry. An\\naligned ordinary-RAM store can leave MEM once its address, byte enables\\nand replicated write data are irrevocably captured. Give a ready bus the\\nstore directly when the entry is empty. If the bus stalls, retain the\\ntransaction and let independent instructions and verified cache hits\\npass. If a second RAM store is waiting when the first is acknowledged,\\nreplace the entry on that edge. Retire each store once, in program order.\\n\\nUpdate the load buffer when MEM accepts ownership of a store. Allocate a\\nfull-word store directly. For SB or SH, probe the resolved row and merge\\nthe enabled bytes only on an exact resident tag hit with a usable read.\\nOtherwise invalidate the index. This lets a younger load observe the\\nstore while the external write waits. Keep the same-index read/write\\nveto on both probes. A demand miss or MMIO access waits its turn on the\\nexternal port. Drain older writes before allowing FENCE.I to invalidate\\nfetc\n…[6159 of 9231 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:ae68a5f99be044e0]…\nlowed by FENCE.I and a stalled refetch.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 278.01, \"delta_pct\": -2.18, \"vs_baseline\": 2193.81, \"fmax_mhz\": 84.511, \"ipc_coremark\": 3e-06, \"cycles\": 3039851, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3833, \"ff\": 1195, \"seeds\": [81.065, 84.511, 84.511], \"perturbations\": [[0, 81.065, 13], [1, 84.511, 12], [2, 84.511, 12]], \"lutram\": 42, \"bsram\": 17, \"dsp\": 4, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_if/reset_q_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/fallthrough_q_30_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -7.336, \"arrival_ns\": 17.63, \"logic_cells\": 13, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_if\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 13, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-21T05:59:05.907505Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 13, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-002-r13s1 (regression, -2.18%): Posting one RAM store let MEM serve load-buffer hits during write stalls, saving 41,754 cycles (1.35%) over ten CoreMark iterations, too little to offset the drop in median Fmax from 87.580 to 84.511 MHz.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
