{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -c 5000 .tmp/agent-logs/impl.hyp-20261121-003-r13s2.log'", "aggregated_output": "ch/test/test_pipeline.py\\n# Outcome-specific successor prediction\\n\\nIF uses the existing 64-entry agree counter and legal control-transfer decode to select one of two rows for each predecessor index. Each row stores the transferred successor's 18-bit word address and raw instruction. Two presence maps permit independent training and a shared 512-clock invalidation sweep.\\n\\nThe trainer retains the previous aligned RAM transfer through bubbles and data-bus holds. It registers the successor payload, bank, predecessor index and write enable before updating the memories. The sequential-address comparison retains the carry out of the RAM address, so a jump from the last RAM word to zero trains the taken row. A simultaneous read of the physical write address misses. Both banks become inaccessible at reset or FENCE.I, and the sweep discards any old fill before lookup resumes.\\n\\nThe pipeline tests exercise both directions with the instruction bus withheld, including the first taken recurrence after a loop exit. They also cover simultaneous writes to the same and opposite bank at one index, a held load, wrong-path stores, and a pending fill for a self-modifying target at FENCE.I. The same-row collision fixture has four loop instructions to align its read with the new physical write cycle.\\n\\nThe payload includes two predecoded bank choices, one for each possible direction-counter high bit. IF selects between them using the current counter. The fall-through presence map uses block RAM. The taken presence map uses four 128-bit distributed memories with registered outputs. EX qualifies its direction and full-target recovery checks before registering them. IF also registers both upper-half sums for PC+4 and selects them with the registered low-half carry.\\n\\nVerilator lint and all 116 cocotb cases passed, including 42 pipeline cases. Co-simulation matched the ISS on selftest and all three random programs with and without stalls. The ten-iteration CoreMark run with both buses stalling took 3,055,382 bracketed cycles, saving \n…[1928 of 5000 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:10082646a943e9e1]…\nrv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep3/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261121-003-r13s2/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\",\"kind\":\"update\"}],\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_169\",\"type\":\"file_change\",\"changes\":[{\"path\":\"/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep3/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261121-003-r13s2/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\",\"kind\":\"update\"}],\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_170\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"[Implementation notes](cores/bench/implementation_notes.md)\\n\\nLint, all 53 formal checks, all 116 cocotb cases, and co-simulation passed.\\n\\nCoreMark took 3,055,382 bracketed cycles with all five CRCs correct. Median Fmax was 87.915 MHz, yielding **287.74 iterations/s**, 1.24% above the champion and below the promotion threshold.\"}}\n{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":11837579,\"cached_input_tokens\":11668992,\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":55103,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":33475}}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
