{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'micro_opt|four-pass|divider' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "1:{\"id\": \"baseline-bench-4f20506\", \"title\": \"Baseline retest for cores/bench\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 12.12, \"delta_pct\": 0.0, \"vs_baseline\": 0.0, \"fmax_mhz\": 5.442, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 12312, \"ff\": 460, \"seeds\": [5.14, 5.442, 5.442], \"perturbations\": [[0, 5.14, 150], [1, 5.442, 149], [2, 5.442, 149]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -189.542, \"arrival_ns\": 199.837, \"logic_cells\": 156, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 150, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-20T19:41:40.095875Z\", \"round_id\": 0, \"slot\": 0}\n2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261120-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Resolve two quotient bits per combinational divider stage\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline runs at a median 5.442 MHz. Its reported 199.837 ns path traverses\\noperand forwarding and the EX ALU. The signed and unsigned division and remainder\\noperators in alu.sv are the strongest candidates for that depth. A shorter\\ncombinational divider could raise Fmax even on cycles executing an ordinary ADD.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline runs at a median 5.442 MHz. Its reported 199.837 ns path traverses\\noperand forwarding and the EX ALU. The signed and unsigned division and remainder\\noperators in alu.sv are the strongest candidates for that depth. A shorter\\ncombinational divider could raise Fmax even on cycles executing an ordinary ADD.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Implement DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU with one unrolled radix-4 magnitude divider\\nin the existing EX cycle. Each of 16 stages consumes the next two dividend bits\\nand produces two quotient bits. For trial remainder T = 4*R + next_pair,\\nform T-D, T-2D and T-3D in parallel. Use their borrow bits to select the\\nlargest fitting multiple and its already-computed difference, pass\n…[9621 of 12693 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:cac166b20c07dec9]…\ntire orders.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 70.74, \"delta_pct\": 483.66, \"vs_baseline\": 483.66, \"fmax_mhz\": 31.773, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 2844, \"ff\": 562, \"seeds\": [31.804, 31.773, 31.773], \"perturbations\": [[0, 31.804, 46], [1, 31.773, 47], [2, 31.773, 47]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_31_s1\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_11_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -26.442, \"arrival_ns\": 36.737, \"logic_cells\": 238, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 46, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-20T19:51:58.943450Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-002-r1s1 (improvement, +483.66%): Splitting DIV/REM across four registered passes shortened the EX timing path to eight quotient decisions per pass, and the timed CoreMark loop incurred no divider stalls because it executes neither operation.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md schemas/hypothesis.schema.json formal/checks_si.cfg'","aggregated_output":"- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-001-r1s0 (regression, +21.70%): Resolving two quotient bits per stage raised median Fmax from 5.442 to 6.627 MHz, but 16 serial remainder selections still limited the EX clock even though the timed CoreMark loop executes no divides.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-002-r1s1 (improvement, +483.66%): Splitting DIV/REM across four registered passes shortened the EX timing path to eight quotient decisions per pass, and the timed CoreMark loop incurred no divider stalls because it executes neither operation.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r1s2 (regression, +11.14%): The 64-entry agree predictor and direct JAL prediction in IF saved 297,001 CoreMark cycles by avoiding one-cycle EX redirect bubbles, while the critical path through forwarding and the EX ALU still limited median Fmax to 5.648 MHz.\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"id\",\"title\",\"category\",\"motivation\",\"hypothesis\",\"expected_impact\",\"changes\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\":       {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^hyp-[0-9]{8}-[0-9]{3}(-r[0-9]+s[0-9]+)?$\"},\n    \"title\":    {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\n# the full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\n# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nalways @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n\n[verilog-files]\n# run_all.sh rebuilds this section from the actual rtl/ glob; the list\n# below is overwritten before genchecks runs. Kept as a placeholder so\n# the section is syntactically present for any reader inspecting the cfg.\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/core.sv\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
