he EX ALU. The signed and unsigned division and remainder\\noperators in alu.sv are the strongest candidates for that depth. A shorter\\ncombinational divider could raise Fmax even on cycles executing an ordinary ADD.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Implement DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU with one unrolled radix-4 magnitude divider\\nin the existing EX cycle. Each of 16 stages consumes the next two dividend bits\\na\n5:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261120-001-r2s0\", \"title\": \"Shorten the divider feedback path to five quotient bits per clock\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The 31.773 MHz champion's reported 36.737 ns worst path runs\n…[14631 of 17703 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f984950fee741be6]…\nligned taken transfers.\\n'}], 'outcome': 'regression', 'fitness': 75.16, 'delta_pct': 6.25, 'vs_baseline': 520.13, 'fmax_mhz': 31.421, 'ipc_coremark': 2e-06, 'cycles': 4180499, 'iterations': 10, 'lut4': 3326, 'ff': 712, 'seeds': [31.47, 31.421, 31.421], 'perturbations': [[0, 31.47, 46], [1, 31.421, 47], [2, 31.421, 47]], 'lutram': 8, 'bsram': 7, 'dsp': 6, 'critical_path': {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_3_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_0_s1', 'slack_ns': -26.776, 'arrival_ns': 37.071, 'logic_cells': 236, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu']}, 'logic_levels': 46, 'formal_passed': True, 'cosim_passed': True, 'error': None, 'implementation_notes': '', 'timestamp': '2026-11-20T20:27:52.330500Z', 'slot': 2, 'round_id': 2, 'lesson': \"- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r2s2 (regression, +6.25%): Caching targets by fetch PC cut CoreMark JALR redirects from 13,735 to 1,647 in the 128-entry BTB prototype, but shortening the four-pass divider's critical path delivered a larger throughput gain (+47.44%).\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
