{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_123","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat 'cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-001-r7s0.yaml'\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261120-001-r7s0\ntitle: Scale the dividend ahead of the reciprocal multiply\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  Gowin traces the champion's longest setup path from the reciprocal seed ROM\n  to quotient_q[5]. The quotient capture currently puts a variable right shift\n  after a 36-by-36 multiply. Its shift count is known four clocks before it\n  is used. At the champion's 3,444,219 cycles for ten iterations, the 4.6%\n  acceptance margin requires just over 74.36 MHz.\nhypothesis: |\n  For nonzero divisor magnitude B, let k = floor(log2(B)). While the shared\n  DSP refines the reciprocal, register A >> k from the unsigned dividend\n  magnitude A. In pass 5 multiply that registered value by the final\n  reciprocal and capture product[65:34] directly as the trial quotient.\n  Pass 6 still computes the residual against the original A and B and\n  applies the existing one-step correction on result selection.\n\n  The early shift rounds down. The existing reciprocal also rounds down\n  and contributes less than 0.91 quotient units of error before binary\n  scaling for any 32-bit A. At exponent k the total underestimate before\n  integer truncation is at most (2^k - 1 + 0.91) / 2^k, strictly below\n  one. Thus the trial quotient is exact or one low. The change removes\n  the barrel shifter from the DSP output path while preserving the seven\n  busy clocks and the one-product-per-clock MEM multiply path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      Register the shifted dividend during the reciprocal refinement using\n      the saved k. Select it as the zero-extended first DSP operand in pass\n      5. Take the fixed high slice for quotient_q. Retain original magnitudes\n      for residual correction, divide-by-zero handling and sign restoration.\n      Preserve the issue, ALTOPS and held-result handshakes.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Exercise divisors just above powers of two across the exponent range,\n      with dividends one below, equal to and one above exact multiples.\n      Include cases with discarded dividend bits all set. Check quotient\n      and remainder against integer arithmetic at the seven-clock latency.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
