vider\\nin the existing EX cycle. Each of 16 stages consumes the next two dividend bits\\nand produces two quotient bits. For trial remainder T = 4*R + next_pair,\\nform T-D, T-2D and T-3D in parallel. Use their borrow bits to select the\\nlargest fitting multiple and its already-computed difference, passing T through\\nfo\n…[9604 of 12676 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:50c90f4bbfd026cf]…\ntire orders.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 70.74, \"delta_pct\": 483.66, \"vs_baseline\": 483.66, \"fmax_mhz\": 31.773, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 2844, \"ff\": 562, \"seeds\": [31.804, 31.773, 31.773], \"perturbations\": [[0, 31.804, 46], [1, 31.773, 47], [2, 31.773, 47]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_31_s1\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_11_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -26.442, \"arrival_ns\": 36.737, \"logic_cells\": 238, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 46, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-20T19:51:58.943450Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-002-r1s1 (improvement, +483.66%): Splitting DIV/REM across four registered passes shortened the EX timing path to eight quotient decisions per pass, and the timed CoreMark loop incurred no divider stalls because it executes neither operation.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
