{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_49","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'ls -a \"$TMPDIR/redirect-fetch-lmlel6ao/test\" && tail -5 \"$TMPDIR/redirect-fetch-lmlel6ao/timing_clean/gowin_p1/gw.log\" && cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-002-r3s1.yaml'","aggregated_output":".\n..\n__pycache__\n_helpers.py\nconftest.py\ntest_alu.py\ntest_decoder.py\ntest_imm_gen.py\ntest_pipeline.py\ntest_pipeline_runner.result.xml\ntest_reg_file.py\n[50%] Placement Phase 3 completed\nRunning routing......\n[60%] Routing Phase 0 completed\n[70%] Routing Phase 1 completed\n[80%] Routing Phase 2 completed\nid: hyp-20261120-002-r3s1\ntitle: Fetch the resolved target in the EX redirect cycle\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion takes 4,491,485 cycles for ten CoreMark iterations at\n  46.846 MHz. On every taken branch, JAL or JALR, EX already has the\n  target while IF presents the sequential PC and discards the returned\n  word. The instruction bus returns the word at the address presented\n  in the current cycle. Using that slot for the target can recover a\n  cycle even for an indirect jump whose address depends on forwarding.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a bypass from the resolved EX target to the instruction address port.\n  Select the target on an aligned taken redirect and the registered fetch\n  PC otherwise. Use this selected address for both io_imemAddr and the\n  instruction's PC in ID. If the front end accepts the word, advance the\n  fetch PC to the selected address plus four. If a redirect coincides with\n  a stall, save the target itself for retry. A ready target can thus enter\n  ID/EX on the same edge that its branch enters EX/MEM.\n\n  A scratch prototype completed ten CRC-validated iterations in 4,136,096\n  marker-bracketed cycles with both stall generators enabled, saving\n  355,389 cycles (7.91%). Gowin placement options 0, 1 and 2 reached\n  46.222, 46.659 and 46.659 MHz. The median gives 112.81 iterations/s\n  (+8.16% over 104.30). The prototype also passed the existing pipeline\n  suite. The timing risk is the path from forwarded branch operands through\n  address selection and the PC increment. At the measured cycle count,\n  a median above 45.124 MHz clears the 4.6% acceptance margin.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: high\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Drive imem_addr and out.pc from the same redirect_target/pc mux.\n      After reset, update the PC in this priority order. On an unstalled\n      transfer, store imem_addr + 4. On a stalled redirect, store the\n      target. Otherwise hold. Use fetch readiness to qualify out.instr\n      and out.valid. A ready word returned on redirect belongs to the target.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Remove the redirect input. Make flush_if depend only on an imem wait.\n      Make flush_id depend on a\n      load-use hazard when the older memory operation can advance. Preserve\n      the dmem and divider holds. A branch held in EX behind a memory wait\n      keeps presenting its target until ID/EX can accept it.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Drop the redirect connection from the hazard-unit instantiation.\n      EX already supplies IF with the alignment-checked redirect and target.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      With both buses ready, check that a forwarded JALR and the instruction\n      at its target retire on adjacent cycles with the correct link and PCs.\n      Exercise a target fetch across an imem wait and a taken branch held\n      behind an older dmem wait. Check consecutive channel-0 orders, exactly\n      one accepted target store, and zero accepted wrong-path stores.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
