{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_47", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -o 'DONE \\\\(PASS|DONE \\\\(FAIL' /srv/hwebench/tmp/ec844b20/affad599/mem-product.97124V/formal-summary.log | sort | uniq -c && cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-002-r5s1.yaml\"", "aggregated_output": "     48 DONE (PASS\nid: hyp-20261120-002-r5s1\ntitle: \"Pipeline RV32M products through MEM and reuse the multiplier for division\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion takes 3,408,562 cycles for ten iterations at 48.072 MHz.\n  Gowin reports a 27.067 ns path from the register file through the EX ALU\n  to data RAM. The five-step divider feedback path reached 25.389 ns on\n  the related load-forwarding design. Round 4's shared multiplier removed\n  both arithmetic paths and reached 61.695 MHz, but holding EX for every\n  multiply added 188,431 cycles to its parent. An earlier MEM-stage multiply\n  trial on that parent added only 35,569 cycles. The timed loop has no divides.\nhypothesis: |\n  Give MEM a single registered-input, signed 36-by-36 multiplier. EX captures\n  forwarded operands on every admitted multiply. MEM computes the product in\n  parallel with the next instruction's EX, and MEM/WB captures its selected\n  word. Independent multiplies can issue every clock. An immediate consumer\n  of the product takes one load-style interlock and forwards from WB.\n\n  During a divide, reuse this same multiplier for two fixed-point Newton\n  reciprocal refinements and a final exact remainder check. Keep the existing\n  seven busy clocks and blocking divide protocol. An older MUL in MEM can\n  finish on the divide issue edge, before the divider needs the multiplier.\n  This removes both the combinational EX products and the five serial\n  subtract/select steps per divide clock.\n\n  A scratch prototype on the champion RTL took 3,444,219 bracketed cycles\n  for ten iterations with both bus stalls enabled. It passed all five CRCs.\n  Gowin placed it at 55.741, 59.704 and 59.704 MHz using two DSP blocks.\n  The median gives 173.35 iterations/s, 22.9% above the champion. The 35,657\n  extra cycles cost 1.05%. At that cycle count the acceptance threshold is\n  50.81 MHz.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 23\n  confidence: high\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      Implement one signed 36x36 product with a full 72-bit\n…[2519 of 5591 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:8e9e2f9d612f03ba]…\n so WB uses the existing write and forwarding path.\n      Keep multiply completion independent of dmemReady and preserve the\n      retained WB forwarding payload when a subsequent memory access waits.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Exercise the registered multiply interface every clock, alternating\n      signed, mixed and unsigned high products with low products. Compare\n      against integer arithmetic. Extend the seven-cycle divide checks to\n      seed-bin edges, divisors near powers of two and dividends on either\n      side of exact multiples. Check zero, overflow and held results.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Check adjacent retirement of independent MULs and one dependency bubble\n      for MUL-to-ADD and MUL-to-MUL. Cover MUL-to-DIV, an independent MUL\n      followed by DIV, DIV-to-MUL, and a MUL held behind a stalled load then\n      consumed by a stalled store. Check channel-0 order, original source\n      values, exact results and a single accepted store.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat >> /srv/hwebench/tmp/ec844b20/affad599/mem-product.97124V/test/test_pipeline.py <<'PY'\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def multiply_pipeline_throughput_and_division(dut):\n    mask = (1 << 32) - 1\n    def mul(rd, a, b, mode=0):\n        return _r(1, b, a, mode, rd, 0x33)\n    insns = [\n        ADDI(1,0,-9), ADDI(2,0,5), mul(3,1,2), mul(4,1,2,1),\n        mul(5,3,2,2), mul(6,5,2,3), DIV(7,2,6), mul(8,7,2),\n        DIV(9,2,1), mul(10,2,1), ADD(11,10,2), EBREAK(),\n    ]\n    rets, _ = await _run(dut, insns)\n    assert [r[\\\"insn\\\"] for r in rets] == insns\n    assert [r[\\\"order\\\"] for r in rets] == list(range(len(insns)))\n    assert all(not r[\\\"trap\\\"] for r in rets)\n    assert [r[\\\"rd_wdata\\\"] for r in rets[:-1]] == [x & mask for x in [-9,5,-45,-1,-1,4,1,5,0,-45,-40]]\n    for i, gap in [(3,1),(4,1),(5,2),(6,10),(7,1),(8,9),(9,1),(10,2)]:\n        assert rets[i][\\\"cycle\\\"] - rets[i-1][\\\"cycle\\\"] == gap\n    for i, a, b in [(4,-45,5), (5,-1,5), (6,5,4), (7,1,5)]:\n        assert (rets[i][\\\"rs1_rdata\\\"], rets[i][\\\"rs2_rdata\\\"]) == (a & mask, b & mask)\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def multiply_across_memory_stalls(dut):\n    mul = _r(1, 2, 1, 0, 3, 0x33)\n    insns = [ADDI(1,0,6), ADDI(2,0,7), LW(4,0,64), mul, SW(3,0,68), EBREAK()]\n    reads, writes = [], []\n    def ready(ren, wen, addr, data):\n        if ren:\n            reads.append(addr)\n            return len(reads) == 4\n        if wen:\n            writes.append((addr,wen,data))\n            return len(writes) == 3\n        return False\n    rets, dmem = await _run(dut, insns, dmem_ready=ready)\n    assert [r[\\\"insn\\\"] for r in rets] == insns\n    assert [r[\\\"order\\\"] for r in rets] == list(range(len(insns)))\n    assert (rets[3][\\\"rs1_rdata\\\"],rets[3][\\\"rs2_rdata\\\"],rets[3][\\\"rd_wdata\\\"]) == (6,7,42)\n    assert reads == [64]*4 and writes == [(68,15,42)]*3\n    assert dmem[68] == 42\nPY\npytest -q --rootdir=. test/test_pipeline.py > pipeline.log 2>&1\ntest_status=\"'$?\ntail -25 pipeline.log\nexit \"$test_status\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
