.165 MHz,\\nbut dependent consumers raised the cycle count to 4,230,003. That left\\nfitness at\n15:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261120-002-r5s1\", \"title\": \"Pipeline RV32M products through MEM and reuse the multiplier for division\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The champion takes 3,408,562 cycles for ten iterations at 48.072 MHz.\\nGowin reports a 27.067 ns path from the register file through the EX ALU\\nto data RAM. The five-step divider feedback path reached 25.389 ns on\\nthe related load-forwarding design. Round 4's shared multiplier removed\\\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
