{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_12", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json,pprint\nds=[json.loads(s) for s in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')]\npprint.pprint(ds[-2],width=160)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "{'bsram': 9,\n 'category': 'structural',\n 'changes': [{'description': 'Implement one signed 36x36 product with a full 72-bit result. Capture\\n'\n                             'sign- or zero-extended MUL operands at EX issue according to the opcode,\\n'\n                             'then take bits 31:0 or 63:32 in MEM. MULHSU sign-extends only rs1.\\n'\n                             'Route the product to a separate MEM output. Keep the integer ALU output\\n'\n                             'and effective-address path independent of the multiplier.\\n'\n                             '\\n'\n                             'For division capture unsigned magnitudes A and B and sign flags on issue.\\n'\n                             'On busy clock 1 normalize nonzero B to D = B << clz(B), save k =\\n'\n                             '31 - clz(B), and seed R = floor(4096*512/(513+D[30:22])) << 22\\n'\n                             'from a constant ROM. Let S = 2^34. On clocks 2 and 4 form D*R and\\n'\n                             'latch E = 2*S - 1 - floor(D*R/2^31). On clocks 3 and 5 latch\\n'\n                             'R = floor(R*E/S). On clock 6 latch Q = floor(A*R/S) >> k. On clock\\n'\n                             '7 latch T = A - Q*B. Use explicitly widened products and zero-extend\\n'\n                             'all division factors into the signed DSP ports. E fits in 35 unsigned\\n'\n                             'bits. Multiplex the two DSP inputs between the registered MUL operands\\n'\n                             'and the registered division factors selected by busy and pass number.\\n'\n                             '\\n'\n                             'The seed underestimates the reciprocal of D/2^31 with relative error at\\n'\n                             'most 1/512 + 2/4096. Each refinement stays below the exact reciprocal\\n'\n                             'and bounds relative error by the previous error squared plus 3/S.\\n'\n                             'After two refinements the quotient error before truncation is below\\n'\n                     \n…[12721 of 15793 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:172908bad5c8a35d]…\norwarding.',\n 'logic_levels': 15,\n 'lut4': 3268,\n 'lutram': 12,\n 'motivation': 'The champion takes 3,408,562 cycles for ten iterations at 48.072 MHz.\\n'\n               'Gowin reports a 27.067 ns path from the register file through the EX ALU\\n'\n               'to data RAM. The five-step divider feedback path reached 25.389 ns on\\n'\n               \"the related load-forwarding design. Round 4's shared multiplier removed\\n\"\n               'both arithmetic paths and reached 61.695 MHz, but holding EX for every\\n'\n               'multiply added 188,431 cycles to its parent. An earlier MEM-stage multiply\\n'\n               'trial on that parent added only 35,569 cycles. The timed loop has no divides.\\n',\n 'outcome': 'improvement',\n 'perturbations': [[0, 58.79, 15], [1, 60.061, 16], [2, 60.061, 16]],\n 'round_id': 5,\n 'seeds': [58.79, 60.061, 60.061],\n 'slot': 1,\n 'timestamp': '2026-11-20T21:27:30.503430Z',\n 'title': 'Pipeline RV32M products through MEM and reuse the multiplier for division',\n 'vs_baseline': 1338.78}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
