aving it for retry on stalls eliminated the taken-redirect bubble, cutting CoreMark cycles by 7.91%.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r3s2 (improvement, +13.68%): Latching the direction IF used and the alternate PC f\n…[1563 of 4635 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:1cb3192edec0e1bc]…\ne EX path and let independent multiplies issue every clock, while an immediate product consumer needed just one stall before WB forwarding.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r5s2 (regression, +15.69%): Probing the word buffer in ID with low bits from an in-flight base producer let EX verify the full address and forward hits without a load-use bubble, saving 192,354 cycles over register-file-only indexing in ten CoreMark iterations.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-001-r6s0 (improvement, +18.37%): Reading the register file asynchronously from distributed RAM while decode resolves forwarding priority lets ID/EX capture each operand and its one-hot select together, shortening the EX path to data RAM without adding a bypass cycle.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r6s2 (regression, +14.56%): Predicting a result-buffer hit from the load PC let dependent consumers use the saved formatted value in EX while MEM checked the tag and format, saving 181,571 CoreMark cycles over the same buffer with an unconditional load-use interlock.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
