{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_54","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nfor r in map(json.loads,Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()):\n if r['id'].endswith(('r2s1','r5s0')):\n  print(r['id'],r['outcome'],r.get('error'),r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'][-1700:])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_54","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nfor r in map(json.loads,Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()):\n if r['id'].endswith(('r2s1','r5s0')):\n  print(r['id'],r['outcome'],r.get('error'),r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'][-1700:])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"hyp-20261120-002-r2s1 regression None Reuse a chain of five restoring quotient-bit steps for seven clocks per\ndivide. Prepend three zero bits to the 32-bit dividend magnitude so all\nseven passes use the same wiring. Register the partial quotient and\nremainder after each pass. This removes three dependent 32-bit\nsubtract-and-select steps from the feedback path at the cost of three\nadditional clocks per DIV, DIVU, REM or REMU.\n\nExpect about 43 MHz median and about 4.49 million bracketed cycles for\nten iterations, or roughly 96 iterations/s. Setup divides may shift the\nphase of the bus stalls. At the champion's cycle count, 33.24 MHz clears\nthe 4.6% acceptance margin. Check the new worst path in Gowin because\nforwarding through the combinational multiplier could limit the gain.\n\nhyp-20261120-001-r5s0 regression None Compare the two source fields of the fetched instruction with the load\ndestination in EX. For an RV32I consumer, latch the matches as two bits\nalongside the consumer in ID/EX. On the next cycle each bit can select\nthe formatted MEM load value directly. This overlaps dependency detection\nwith address generation and lets a ready load and its consumer advance on\nconsecutive edges. Keep the load interlock for an immediately dependent\nRV32M instruction so the multiplier receives registered producer data.\nGive memory operations their own registered base-plus-immediate address\nto keep the multiply result mux out of the data RAM address path.\n\nAn isolated prototype on the current champion ran ten CRC-validated\niterations in 3,204,188 bracketed cycles with both stall generators\nenabled, saving 204,374 cycles. Gowin placements 0, 1 and 2 reached\n50.935, 52.031 and 52.031 MHz. The median gives 162.38 iterations/s,\n15.14% above 141.03. At that cycle count, 47.27 MHz clears the acceptance\nmargin. Divider feedback now sets the longest path. A load-to-fetch\ncontrol path is within 0.06 ns of it on placement 1.\n\nAll 53 fast formal checks passed. The selftest and three random programs\nmatched the reference with ready and stalled buses. Directed pipeline\ntests also passed for a saved consumer behind a waiting load, a trapping\nload shadowing an older writer, and a load followed by MULH.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
