{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_87", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-002-r7s1.yaml')\np.write_text(\\\"\\\"\\\"id: hyp-20261120-002-r7s1\ntitle: Give Newton division dedicated registered product paths\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  Gowin traced the champion's 19.855 ns worst path from the reciprocal\n  seed ROM to the quotient register. The other round-six operand design\n  had the same endpoints. Four kinds of divider product and ordinary MUL\n  all use one 36x36 multiplier, with input steering and a variable shift\n  on the quotient output. This limits the 71.092 MHz clock even though\n  the timed CoreMark loop executes no divides.\nhypothesis: |\n  Dedicate one registered-input multiplier to ordinary MUL and give the\n  blocking divider four separately inferred products with fixed operand\n  sources. Two products implement the two Newton refinements, one estimates\n  the quotient, and one computes Q*B for exact correction. While the\n  reciprocal refines, pre-shift dividend magnitude A by the divisor\n  exponent k and precompute A-B. The quotient product then feeds a fixed\n  bit slice. The residual product feeds two parallel subtractors whose\n  registered outputs supply both possible remainders and the correction\n  bit. This keeps the seven divide clocks and one multiply issue per clock.\n+\n  For nonzero divisor magnitude B let D = B / 2\"'^k, k = floor(log2(B)),\n  S = 2''^34 and r = R/S after refinement. The existing 512-bin seed has\n  relative error below 1/512 + 2/4096. Each rounded Newton step keeps a\n  lower bound and maps relative error e to at most e''^2 + 3/S. After two\n  steps, 0 <= 1/D - r < 2''^-32. Discarding the low k bits of A costs at\n  most 1 - 2''^-k quotient units, and the reciprocal error on A >> k costs\n  less than 2''^-k. The trial Q is exact or one low. The sign of (A-B)-Q*B\n  therefore selects the exact quotient and remainder using one correction.\n+\n  In scratch timing trials, registering the inputs of the shared multiplier\n  and moving the dividend shift reached a 73.761 MHz median. Giving the\n  products fixed operand sources reached 74.865 MHz. Registering both\n  residual candidates reached 77.380 MHz on placement 1, with the worst\n  path now in instruction fetch. At the champion'\"'s 3,444,219 bracketed\n  cycles for ten iterations, 74.37 MHz clears the acceptance margin.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 9\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      Keep the ordinary signed 36x36 product directly on the two MUL\n      operand registers. Capture signed extensions according to MULH,\n      MULHSU or MULHU and select the existing MEM high/low word. Capture\n      magnitudes A and B, sign, zero and result-kind flags on divide issue.\n      Infer four unsigned products directly from registers. They are\n      normalized_B[31:0] * R[33:0], factor[34:0] * R[33:0],\n      X[31:0] * R[33:0], and the low 32 bits of Q[31:0] * B[31:0].\n      On pass 0 capture normalized B, k and the current 12-bit seed\n      shifted left 22. On passes 1 and 3 capture the complement of bits\n      [65:31] of the first product as factor. On passes 2 and 4 capture\n      bits [67:34] of the second as R. In parallel, register zero-extended\n      A minus zero-extended B in 33 bits on pass 1 and X = A >> k on\n      pass 2. Pass 5 captures Q from bits [65:34] of the third product.\n      Pass 6 captures A-Q*B in 32 bits and (A-B)-Q*B in 33 bits. A clear\n      bit 32 in the latter selects its low word for REM and increments Q\n      for DIV. Apply the existing result sign and division-by-zero rules.\n      Hold results through backpressure and retain the common request,\n      result-valid and ALTOPS timing.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Cover all 32 divisor exponents with dividends just below, at and\n      above exact multiples and with all k discarded bits set. Check DIVU\n      and REMU against integer divmod, including held responses. Issue\n      MULHSU, DIVU and MULHU consecutively at their legal issue edges to\n      exercise the separate operand registers. Keep the existing signed\n      corner, reciprocal-bin, multiply-throughput and latency checks.\n\\\"\\\"\\\".replace('\\\\n+\\\\n','\\\\n\\\\n'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
