{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'predictor|hyp-20261120-002-r1s1' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261120-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Move DIV and REM to a shared four-pass divider\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The 5.442 MHz baseline takes 4,491,485 cycles for ten CoreMark iterations.\\nGowin reports a 199.837 ns, 156-cell path through forwarding and the EX ALU.\\nThe ALU evaluates full-width signed and unsigned division and remainder\\ncombinationally. Their serial quotient decisions are the likeliest source\\nof this depth. Disassembly of the canonical RV32IM -O3 ELF shows five\\nDIVU instructions, all in main. The measured start_time/iterate/stop_time\\nsequence executes none of them, and the ELF contains no DIV, REM or REMU.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The 5.442 MHz baseline takes 4,491,485 cycles for ten CoreMark iterations.\\nGowin reports a 199.837 ns, 156-cell path through forwarding and the EX ALU.\\nThe ALU evaluates full-width signed and unsigned division and remainder\\ncombinationally. Their serial quotient decisions are the likeliest source\\nof this depth. Disassembly of the canonical RV32IM -O3 ELF shows five\\nDIVU instructions, all in main. The measured start_time/iterate/stop_time\\nsequence executes none of them, and the ELF contains no DIV, REM or REMU.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Give EX one blocking divider for DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU. Latch forwarded\\noperands on issue, divide their unsigned magnitudes with eight restoring\\nquotient-bit steps per clock for four clocks, then select and sign-correct\\nthe quotient or remainder. Use the subtraction borrow to select the next\\nremainder at each step. The register between passes cuts the full-width\\nrecurrence out of the one-cycle ALU path. Only division and remainder add\\nissue stalls, so matrix multiplies and ordinary integer dependencies can\\nsustain their current issue rate.\\n\\nExpect nearly the same marker-bracketed cycle count. Extra divide cycles\\nduring setup can shift the phase of the pseudo-random bus stalls. At the\\nbaseline cycle count, 8.163 MHz would yield a 50% fitness gain. Even with\\n2% more cycles, 5.81 MHz would clear\n…[12376 of 15448 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:8ac7c4e2ce2359af]…\nession\", \"fitness\": 13.47, \"delta_pct\": 11.14, \"vs_baseline\": 11.14, \"fmax_mhz\": 5.648, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4194484, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 12649, \"ff\": 463, \"seeds\": [5.223, 5.648, 5.648], \"perturbations\": [[0, 5.223, 153], [1, 5.648, 154], [2, 5.648, 154]], \"lutram\": 12, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_0_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -186.458, \"arrival_ns\": 196.752, \"logic_cells\": 166, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 153, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-20T20:07:28.954260Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r1s2 (regression, +11.14%): The 64-entry agree predictor and direct JAL prediction in IF saved 297,001 CoreMark cycles by avoiding one-cycle EX redirect bubbles, while the critical path through forwarding and the EX ALU still limited median Fmax to 5.648 MHz.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
