h the accepted instruction. Direct targets are exact by construction,\\nso EX can detect a miss by comparing this bit with the resolved direction.\\nA miss redirects to the resolved next PC and kills the younger instruction.\\nCorrect predictions let the successor enter ID/EX immediately. An isolated\\nRTL prototype completed ten 2K CoreMark iterations in 4,194,484 bracketed\\ncycles with both bus stalls enabled, versus 4,491,485 on the baseline.\\nAll five CRCs matched. Gowin reported 5.214, 5.486 and 5.486 MHz across\\nthe three placement \n…[12317 of 15389 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:3803cef4ac4d814f]…\n a stale hit. Include an EX correction\\nduring an imem stall, a branch held behind a stalled load, and\\nmisaligned taken transfers.\\n'}]}\noutcome regression\nfitness 75.16\ndelta_pct 6.25\nvs_baseline 520.13\nfmax_mhz 31.421\nipc_coremark 2e-06\ncycles 4180499\niterations 10\nlut4 3326\nff 712\nseeds [31.47, 31.421, 31.421]\nperturbations [[0, 31.47, 46], [1, 31.421, 47], [2, 31.421, 47]]\nlutram 8\nbsram 7\ndsp 6\ncritical_path {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_3_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_0_s1', 'slack_ns': -26.776, 'arrival_ns': 37.071, 'logic_cells': 236, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu']}\nlogic_levels 46\nformal_passed True\ncosim_passed True\nerror None\nimplementation_notes \ntimestamp 2026-11-20T20:27:52.330500Z\nslot 2\nround_id 2\nlesson - 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r2s2 (regression, +6.25%): Caching targets by fetch PC cut CoreMark JALR redirects from 13,735 to 1,647 in the 128-entry BTB prototype, but shortening the four-pass divider's critical path delivered a larger throughput gain (+47.44%).\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
