{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d.get('category')=='predictor' or 'r3s1' in str(d.get('id')):\n  print(d.keys(),d['id']); print(str(d.get('implementation_notes'))[:4100]); print(str(d.get('hypothesis'))[-2600:])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "dict_keys(['id', 'title', 'category', 'motivation', 'hypothesis', 'expected_impact', 'changes', 'outcome', 'fitness', 'delta_pct', 'vs_baseline', 'fmax_mhz', 'ipc_coremark', 'cycles', 'iterations', 'lut4', 'ff', 'seeds', 'perturbations', 'lutram', 'bsram', 'dsp', 'critical_path', 'logic_levels', 'formal_passed', 'cosim_passed', 'error', 'implementation_notes', 'timestamp', 'slot', 'round_id', 'lesson']) hyp-20261120-003-r1s2\n\nth bus stalls enabled, versus 4,491,485 on the baseline.\\nAll five CRCs matched. Gowin reported 5.214, 5.486 and 5.486 MHz across\\nthe three placement options. The median gives 13.08 iter/s, a 7.9% gain\\nover 12.12. The prototype used 12 LUT-RAM primitives versus 8 at baseline.\\n', 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 8, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'description': \"Initialize counters to 01 (weak agreement) at configuration. Use one\\nasynchronous read indexed by the fetch PC and one synchronous write.\\nDecode legal B and JAL from raw imem_data. Calculate the signed target\\nand feed the guarded prediction into the PC mux. Give reset first\\npriority, then an EX correction even if imem is stalled, then the\\nprediction on an accepted fetch. Hold the PC on other stalls.\\nTrain from the resolving branch's\\nsaved counter. Increment on disagreement with the offset sign, decrement\\non agreement, and saturate at either end. When an older branch updates\\nthe index being fetched, bypass the new count into the younger branch's\\ntraining snapshot. Record the direction actually selected for fetch.\\n\"}, {'file': 'rtl/core_pkg.sv', 'description': 'Add predicted_taken and the two-bit counter snapshot to both IF/ID and ID/EX.'}, {'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'description': 'Latch the direction and counter snapshot with the instruction using its hold and bubble controls.'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Resolve branches with forwarded operands as today. Count a taken\\nmisaligned transfer as fall-through for recovery and preserve its trap\\nand link-write suppre\n…[9052 of 12124 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:ecdde09cad07aef2]…\nt with the offset sign and decrement on agreement, with\\nsaturation at both ends.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/hazard_unit.sv', 'description': 'Detect load-use from raw source fields independently of redirect.\\nGive dmem and divider holds priority, inject an ID/EX bubble for an\\nadvancing miss, load-use or unavailable fetch, and let a miss\\noverride the fetch PC hold. Remove redirect-driven instruction masking.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': \"Connect the training write enable, resolving PC index and updated count\\nfrom EX to IF. Drive PC recovery and the hazard unit's squash from the\\nsame advancing EX miss signal.\\n\"}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Check immediate target fetch on a warmed loop, the first exit, a\\nforward branch that learns taken, JAL and JALR. Check retired PCs,\\nlink values and the dmem write mask for wrong-path stores. Exercise\\na miss with imemReady low, a resolving branch held by dmemReady,\\naliasing counters, reserved branches and a misaligned taken target.\\n'}]}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
