{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor x in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if x['id'].endswith(('r4s2','r4s0','r4s1','r3s2')):\n  print(x['id'],x['hypothesis'],x['cycles'], x['fitness'],x['critical_path'],x['bsram'],x['lutram'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261120-003-r3s2 {'motivation': \"The champion spends 4,491,485 cycles on ten CoreMark iterations. A prior\\nfetch-stage agree predictor saved 297,001 cycles on the same workload.\\nThe champion's reported 26.981 ns path now runs from EX/MEM.rd through\\nforwarding, branch resolution, IF instruction masking and hazard logic\\nto ID/EX.rs1_val. Preserving the cycle savings requires keeping branch\\nrecovery off the decode and operand-capture paths.\\n\", 'hypothesis': 'Predict legal conditional branches and JAL at fetch. Index 64 two-bit\\nagree counters with PC[7:2]. The offset sign supplies the default\\ndirection (backward taken), and the counter MSB inverts that direction\\nwhen disagreement predominates. Compute the exact B/J target from the\\nfetched instruction. Select it only when aligned and in instruction RAM.\\nOtherwise select PC+4. JALR uses sequential prediction.\\n\\nLatch the decision actually used and the alternate direct successor in\\nID/EX. A correctly predicted branch admits its successor on the next\\nready fetch. On a miss, the forwarded branch comparison selects recovery\\nwith a one-bit direction check. The alternate address is already\\nregistered. JALR retains its forwarded target calculation in EX. Send\\nthe correction directly to the PC and to the ID/EX bubble control.\\nDecode and load-use detection can consume the raw instruction in\\nparallel because a bubble clears valid and all side-effect controls.\\n\\nAn isolated prototype of this design on the champion completed ten\\niterations in 4,194,434 bracketed cycles with both bus stalls enabled,\\nsaving 297,051 cycles. CoreMark validated all five CRCs. Gowin reported\\n47.124, 47.840 and 47.840 MHz across its three placement options. The\\nmedian gives 114.06 iterations/s, 9.35% above the champion and above the\\n109.10 iterations/s acceptance threshold. The worst reported path in\\noption 0 now runs from the register file through execution to data RAM.\\nThat placement used 2,759 logic cells and 12 LUT-RAM primitives, versus\\n2,643 and eight on the champion\n…[16191 of 19263 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:642c92e19e66f003]…\ntural resolution.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': \"Wire IF's JALR forecast-valid bit and selected fetch address to EX.\\nFeed if_id_w.valid to the hazard unit's fetch-availability input.\\nIF still receives raw io_imemReady to distinguish bus data from a\\nprediction. Keep availability independent of stall_if and redirect.\\n\"}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Warm beyond the reset sweep, withhold imemReady on a learned edge\\nand poison unready bus data. Check adjacent retirement on a JALR hit.\\nChange its target, then supply a misaligned target. Cover colliding\\npredecessor indices, a JALR held behind a stalled load, channel-0\\norder and wrong-path store strobes. Replace a learned word across\\nFENCE.I and verify that fetch waits for the updated word.\\n'}]} 3408562 141.03 {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -16.773, 'arrival_ns': 27.067, 'logic_cells': 16, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']} 8 12\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
