{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_55", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-003-r5s2.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261120-003-r5s2\ntitle: Predict each load's word index from its decode-stage base register\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The successor predictor already supplies 604,950 instructions during\n  CoreMark fetch stalls. The champion still takes 3,408,562 cycles for ten\n  iterations. An immediately dependent instruction waits a cycle for a\n  load, and a data-bus wait holds both instructions. A load PC often sees\n  the same displacement between the base value available in decode and\n  the eventual effective address, even when the base advances each loop.\nhypothesis: |\n  Learn that displacement per load PC and use it to start a synchronous\n  data-word lookup one stage early. Keep 256 untagged 12-bit displacements\n  indexed by PC[9:2]. ID adds the prediction to the low 12 bits of its\n  register-file rs1 read, including the existing WB bypass. Bits [11:2]\n  of this sum index a 1024-word tagged RAM. Save the probed index and the\n  low bits of the base actually used. Train once per completed legal RAM\n  load with (resolved byte address - saved decode base) modulo 4096.\n  This learns both the instruction immediate and a repeatable correction\n  for writes to rs1 that were still in flight at decode.\n\n  In EX, form the full architectural address from forwarded rs1 plus the\n  decoded immediate. Accept the predicted word only if the RAM-region,\n  tag, probed index and access alignment all match. Apply the resolved\n  byte offset, width and signedness. An early hit supplies an EX/MEM\n  forwarding result and admits the immediately dependent instruction.\n  An incorrect prediction retains the demand read and its interlock.\n  Both cases retire one architectural load with the actual aligned\n  address, byte mask and raw word on RVFI.\n\n  Populate a row from an accepted demand read or a full-word store in\n  ordinary RAM. Invalidate it on an accepted partial store. Suppress a\n  same-index probe/write collision and veto an early hit if an older store\n  in MEM has the same index. Sweep all row-valid bits on reset while\n  demand traffic continues. Cold and aliased displacement entries can\n  select any row safely because EX verifies the complete word address.\n\n  With both bus stalls enabled an isolated prototype completed the ten\n  iterations in 3,205,062 bracketed cycles with all five canonical CRCs.\n  Using the instruction immediate as the displacement in the same buffer\n  took 3,251,054 cycles, so learning the displacement saved 45,992 cycles.\n  Gowin's three placement options for the learned predictor reached\n  48.029, 49.326 and 49.326 MHz. The median gives 153.90 iterations/s,\n  9.13% above 141.03. At this cycle count 47.281 MHz clears the acceptance\n  threshold. Placement option zero used 3,680 logic cells and ten BSRAMs.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 9\n  confidence: high\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Add the PC-indexed displacement table and the synchronous word RAM.\n      Each word-buffer row packs valid, address[19:12] and 32 raw data\n      bits. Capture its response, actual probe index and decode base on\n      the ID/EX enable. Hold them through a stall. Carry the base to MEM\n      for training, implement coherent fills and invalidation, and suppress\n      ambiguous RAM collisions. Wire the early result into the existing\n      forwarding and hazard paths. Gate the load-use predicate with a\n      verified EX hit and the data-bus wait with an outstanding request.\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: |\n      Add the effective byte address, predicted raw word and verified-hit\n      bit to EX/MEM. Keep the architectural load controls for retirement.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Register forwarded rs1 plus immediate as the effective address for\n      memory operations. Match the candidate and extract the load value\n      in parallel. Select the extracted value into EX/MEM.alu_result for\n      a load. Only a verified hit releases the load-use interlock, so a\n      miss's speculative value cannot reach a dependent instruction.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Drive the bus address, trap checks and byte masks from the registered\n      effective address. Suppress the demand read on an early hit, use its\n      registered extended value for WB and its saved raw word for RVFI.\n      Supply the ordinary bus read and extension on a miss.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Test a repeating load with an older producer updating its base,\n      then change the producer displacement. Cover PC and data-index\n      aliases, same-row read/write, a stalled partial store, subword sign\n      extension and misalignment. Check hit and miss retirement spacing,\n      RVFI data and masks, and external read counts under backpressure.\nYAML\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
