{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '\\\"predictor\\\"|successor|Predict' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python -c \\\"import json,sys;[(print({k:v for k,v in d.items() if k in ('id','category','title','fitness','fitness_delta_pct','coremark_iter_per_cycle','hypothesis','implementation_notes')})) for l in sys.stdin for d in [json.loads(l.partition(':')[2])]]\\\"\"", "aggregated_output": "{'id': 'hyp-20261120-003-r1s2', 'title': 'Predict direct branches with a 64-entry agree predictor at fetch', 'category': 'predictor', 'hypothesis': {'motivation': \"The baseline fetches PC+4 until EX resolves a transfer. Since IF feeds ID\\ncombinationally, a taken branch or jump discards one younger fetch slot.\\nA reference trace between the CoreMark markers contains 529,588 conditional\\nbranches, of which 294,425 change the successor, plus 49,367 direct jumps.\\nThe baseline's 199.837 ns worst path crosses forwarding and the EX ALU.\\nPredicting these direct transfers in IF can save cycles with a small table.\\n\", 'hypothesis': 'Index 64 two-bit saturating counters with fetch PC[7:2]. Use the offset\\nsign as the default direction for a legal conditional branch (backward\\ntaken, forward fall-through). Predict taken = offset_sign XOR counter[1].\\nThe counter learns whether to invert the default, so a hot backedge and\\na usually untaken forward guard can share an entry constructively. Predict\\ndirect JAL taken. Compute the signed B/J target in parallel with the table\\nlookup and select it only for a word-aligned address in instruction RAM.\\nUse PC+4 for every other fetch, including JALR. Carry the selected direction\\nbit with the accepted instruction. Direct targets are exact by construction,\\nso EX can detect a miss by comparing this bit with the resolved direction.\\nA miss redirects to the resolved next PC and kills the younger instruction.\\nCorrect predictions let the successor enter ID/EX immediately. An isolated\\nRTL prototype completed ten 2K CoreMark iterations in 4,194,484 bracketed\\ncycles with both bus stalls enabled, versus 4,491,485 on the baseline.\\nAll five CRCs matched. Gowin reported 5.214, 5.486 and 5.486 MHz across\\nthe three placement options. The median gives 13.08 iter/s, a 7.9% gain\\nover 12.12. The prototype used 12 LUT-RAM primitives versus 8 at baseline.\\n', 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 8, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'description': \"Initialize co\n…[26635 of 29707 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c3514be166e46815]…\nd and the normal ALU result for other writers. Retain EX/MEM\\npriority over WB and x0 exclusion. The interlock keeps a consumer\\nof a missed load out of EX until WB can supply the demand value.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/mem_stage.sv', 'description': 'Use the registered effective address for the bus, alignment checks\\nand RVFI masks. An early hit suppresses io_dmemREn, writes back the\\nregistered extended value and reports its raw word to RVFI. A miss\\nsamples and extends the accepted data-bus word as before.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'After warmup, run two dependent pointer loads feeding an ADD and\\ncheck three consecutive retirements with the data bus unavailable.\\nGive an ADD producer stale latched operands, delay the true demand\\nread and check that the younger load and consumer use the corrected\\nword. Cover high-address tag aliases, a held partial store to a hot\\nword, subword extension, misalignment, read strobes and RVFI order.\\n'}]}, 'fitness': 163.16, 'implementation_notes': ''}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
