{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_91", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-003-r7s2.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261120-003-r7s2\ntitle: \"Predict the load address in decode and give misses a second probe in execute\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion takes 3,444,219 cycles for ten iterations. Its load-use\n  interlock waits even when the same RAM word has been read many times.\n  An earlier PC-stride trial missed 85,446 dependent accesses at four\n  pointer-chasing sites. Those incorrect predictions can still save a\n  data-bus wait if the load gets a second lookup at its resolved address.\nhypothesis: |\n  Give each load two chances to read one coherent set of RAM words.\n  A small PC-indexed stride predictor supplies the first word index in\n  decode. Store the precomputed next index so this lookup needs no address\n  addition on the decode-to-RAM path. In EX, compare the predicted index\n  and returned tag with the full forwarded effective address. An aligned\n  hit can register the correctly extracted operand for the next instruction\n  and release the load-use interlock. A wrong index costs the ordinary\n  interlock. In parallel, launch a second synchronous read using the\n  resolved word index. A hit there completes the load in MEM and supplies\n  WB, even when the external data bus is stalled. An ordinary demand read\n  covers a double miss. Only a verified address can supply load data.\n\n  The first probe targets dependency bubbles and the second limits the\n  cost of an inaccurate prediction to the lost early bypass. At unchanged\n  frequency, saving 152,000 bracketed cycles clears the acceptance margin.\n  Compare both probes enabled with the same design using the resolved\n  probe alone, and measure the three-placement median to price the extra\n  RAM routing and EX hit check.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Add a 64-entry table indexed by load PC holding the previous word\n      index and predicted next word index. Train on an advancing aligned\n      RAM load using twice its current index minus its previous index\n      modulo 10\n…[1135 of 4207 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:57ae7dbdccb2d9da]…\n agree.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Interlock an immediate load consumer only when the early probe\n      misses. Preserve the multiply interlock and freeze on a waiting\n      external demand. Let verified internal loads advance independently\n      of dmemReady.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Prefer the verified early word, then a verified resolved-probe\n      word, then accepted demand data. Suppress the read strobe on an\n      internal completion. Use the selected raw word for RVFI and for\n      ordinary lane extraction. Preserve trap and store sequencing.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Warm a striding load and check consecutive load-consumer retirements\n      during a data wait. Change the stride to another resident word,\n      then to a cold word, and check the second hit and demand fallback.\n      Exercise colliding predictor PCs, a held partial store, same-row\n      read/write, address-tag aliases, subword formats and misalignment.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
