{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_90", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-001-r11s0.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261121-001-r11s0\ntitle: Read the successor RAM one fetch early and register its response before decode\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  Four of the five longest paths on the champion's 79.301 MHz placement ran from the successor RAM to the fetch PC. The split-target experiment reached 80.074 MHz and put EX forwarding and address generation on the path to the RAM write enable. A scratch implementation that queued the writes and stored an absolute direct target preserved all five CRCs and 3,062,533 bracketed cycles, but reached only 76.294 MHz on placement 1. A register between the RAM output and fetch steering could shorten the read path while keeping training writes off the admission path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Look up the existing 512-row successor table one fetch earlier. While fetching A and predicting B, send B's nine index bits to the synchronous read port. During B the RAM presents the row for B, which contains its previously observed successor C and C's instruction. At the edge admitting B, capture this row in fabric flip-flops. During C, the saved instruction, its address and its direct-target metadata are available from those flip-flops. A warm stream still admits one instruction per clock.\n\n  The lookup is speculative and internal. Use the low bits of the sequential or predicted direct address without waiting for full target-range validation, EX redirect or the load-use interlock. Check the registered probe index against the actual B index before promoting its response. Keep the full word-address check before issuing C from that response. A bad probe costs a cache opportunity. A ready bus can still supply the instruction immediately. Stage accepted training pairs for one clock so the physical write port takes registered inputs.\n\n  The frequency target is 84.5 MHz. At that clock, ten iterations must finish in fewer than 3.120 million bracketed cycles to clear the 4.6 percent promotion margin. The main risks are missed probes after redirects and a new timing path into the nine-bit RAM address.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Retain the successor-table indexing and agree counters. Give the read port a free-running lookahead index. Carry the sampled index and collision validity with its output. Promote a matching row only for an admitted RAM PC. Preserve a usable response across holds, and retry the actual predecessor index on a missed lookahead when fetch is waiting. Keep the admitted successor word stable across repeated waits. A ready bus word overrides cached data and drives its own B/J prediction. Train from a registered predecessor index, successor PC, bus word and enable. Use the write stage to pack the successor instruction's aligned in-RAM B/J target and eligibility bits. Verify legal JALR steering in EX. Invalidate or forward reads that conflict with a pending or intervening write, including a held probe. Preserve the existing logical same-row collision veto. On reset or an admitted FENCE.I discard pending fills, probes and held responses and let the sweep take priority.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      On a direct direction miss, form the recovery PC from the issuing instruction's registered PC and immediate. Choose PC+4 for a predicted-taken miss and the full target for a predicted-fallthrough miss. This lets IF store only the aligned RAM target in a row. Keep the advancing-instruction qualification, JALR target comparison, trap handling and channel-0 retirement behavior.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Exercise a warm direct-branch loop with the instruction bus held low, a redirect whose correct target has a different probe index, and a held probe overwritten before promotion. Cross a 512-row alias and admit FENCE.I with a queued fill. Check fetch recovery, exact channel-0 instructions, PCs, order and store effects, plus consecutive retirements on a warmed correct lookahead.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-001-r11s0.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint(d['id'],d['category'])\nprint(84.5e6*10/(258.94*1.046))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
