{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if not {'r6s0', 'r7s2','r11s0','r11s2', 'r10s0'} & set(d['id'].split('-')): continue\n print(d['id'], d.get('critical_path'),d.get('hypothesis',''),d.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261120-001-r6s0 {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/seed_seed_0_0_s', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_5_s0', 'slack_ns': -9.561, 'arrival_ns': 19.855, 'logic_cells': 10, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu']} {'motivation': 'Gowin reports a 22.304 ns path from register-file block RAM through EX\\nto data RAM on the 60.061 MHz champion. Block RAM supplies the register\\noperand after the decode clock edge. EX also compares producer register\\nnumbers, resolves their priority and selects the operand before doing the\\noperation. Both the operand value and its source can be prepared in decode.\\n', 'hypothesis': 'Read both register operands asynchronously from distributed RAM, apply\\nthe WB write-first bypass and capture them in the existing ID/EX operand\\nregisters. In parallel, compare each fetched source with the destinations\\ncurrently in EX and MEM. Register a three-bit one-hot selection per source\\nat the same edge. In EX, mask and OR the captured operand, EX/MEM ALU\\nresult and MEM/WB write data. Each bypass still delivers its value at the\\noriginal clock. Moving the read and priority decision before the edge\\nshortens the path through EX for memory, arithmetic and branch consumers.\\n\\nAn isolated prototype reached 66.872, 67.927 and 67.927 MHz under the\\nthree Gowin placement options. Distributed register reads alone reached\\na median of 61.800 MHz. Registering the bypass selects alone reached\\n62.744 MHz. The combined median and 3,444,219 bracketed cycles\\nfor ten CRC-validated iterations with both buses stalling give 197.22\\niterations/s, 13.1% above 174.38. Placement zero used 3,331 logic cells,\\n752 registers, seven BSRAMs and two DSPs. Its longest path moved into the\\ndivider. The prototype matched reference retirement on selftest and all\\nthree random programs with zero-wait and stalled buses. All 53 single-retire\\nALTOPS formal checks and 100 cocotb cases passed, including directed\\nsimulations of trapping writers, held bypass data and a second reset\\nafter populating the register file.\\n', 'expected_imp\n…[19969 of 23041 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:2445edf184fe0953]…\nerve sweep invalidation, alignment, RAM bounds, partial\\nstore invalidation, collision handling and MMIO routing.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Compare the expected base supplied by the predictor against the\\ncaptured RF operand, EX/MEM result, registered product and WB word.\\nSelect the equality bit with the registered youngest-writer choice.\\nUse it only to certify the early bypass. Keep the exact effective\\naddress and formatted data paths for the memory operation and RVFI.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Update buffered_xor_miss to require a bubble on the cold access and\\nconsecutive retirement on the second, hot 68+4 access. Keep every\\ndata, bus and order assertion. Exercise both carries at bit 6,\\npositive and negative page crossings, a wrong pointer with the same\\nlow 12 bits, and byte/halfword alignment. Contrast a simultaneous\\nwrite to the other bank with a same-row write, including a held\\nstore. Check exact forwarded values and demand-read counts.\\n'}]} \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
