{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_70","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-001-r12s0.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261121-001-r12s0\ntitle: Remove branch recovery from the instruction data mux\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  On placement 0 the champion's 17.865 ns path starts at wrong_direction_q,\n  crosses fetch and the asynchronous register file, and ends at early_index_q.\n  A redirect changes which saved instruction drives rs1 before the register\n  file and the load-buffer index logic can start. The saved row already has\n  the address needed to check whether its instruction belongs at the recovery PC.\nhypothesis: |\n  Select the candidate instruction independently of branch recovery. On an\n  instruction-bus wait, present the synchronous successor RAM output on a\n  normal slot and the retained response on a held or replayed slot. Use the\n  ready bus word with highest priority. Let redirect choose the actual fetch\n  PC and qualify admission in parallel. On recovery, admit the candidate\n  from RAM only when its valid, collision-qualified full address matches\n  the resolved PC. A miss waits at that PC. Retain the previous response\n  for retry so a correct word held across a stalled branch remains usable\n  even if the first recovery candidate misses. Preserve the forecast address\n  EX checks, reset and FENCE.I invalidation, and the single retirement stream.\n\n  This removes redirect from both register read addresses and the displacement\n  bits used to guess the load-buffer index. The tradeoff is an occasional\n  extra recovery cycle when only the retained word matches and the bus is\n  stalled. At the champion's 3,081,605 cycles, promotion requires a median\n  above 87.49 MHz. Measure both the changed cycle count and the three-placement\n  median since another path can take over.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Decouple the saved instruction data mux from redirect. Qualify its row\n      according to the selected source, use full-address matching on recovery,\n      and retain a matching recovery response across a wait. Keep the word,\n      address and hit qualification aligned through consecutive holds, replays,\n      redirects, read/write collisions and invalidation.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Train distinct words at aliasing fetch indices, then redirect during\n      an instruction wait with different fresh and retained responses.\n      Exercise a match in each source and a full-address miss. Check exact\n      channel-0 PCs, instructions and order, and count accepted stores.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
