{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_99", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nd=next(Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/ec844b20/f7190d73/microopt-ke2ebicx/proof/formal/riscv-formal/cores').glob('bench-*'))/'checks'\nfor x in sorted(d.glob('*.sby')):\n l=x.with_suffix('')/'logfile.txt'\n if not l.is_file(): print(x.stem,'not started')\n elif 'DONE' not in l.read_text(): print(x.stem,l.read_text().splitlines()[-1][-130:])\nPY\ntail -3 /srv/hwebench/tmp/ec844b20/f7190d73/microopt-ke2ebicx/proof/formal/last_run-*.log && cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-001-r12s0.yaml\"", "aggregated_output": "reg_ch0 SBY  4:13:50 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:01:01  waiting for solver (1 minute)\nSBY  4:14:11 [insn_sub_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned pass\nSBY  4:14:11 [insn_sub_ch0] summary: engine_0 did not produce any traces\nSBY  4:14:11 [insn_sub_ch0] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\nid: hyp-20261121-001-r12s0\ntitle: Register the divider product before residual correction\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  On the champion's 83.645 MHz median placement, Gowin reports 17.250 ns\n  from the reciprocal ROM through the shared DSP to residual_q and 17.244 ns\n  from residual_q into the signed divide result register. Pass 6 puts a\n  32-bit subtractor after the DSP. The following cycle can compare, subtract\n  and negate in series. CoreMark executes no divides in its timed loop,\n  but both paths constrain the clock on every instruction.\nhypothesis: |\n  Keep the seven-pass Newton schedule and retime its final correction. Let\n  A and B be the dividend and divisor magnitudes, Q the existing quotient\n  estimate and P = Q*B. For B > 0 the estimate is exact or one low, so\n  P fits in 32 bits. The correction test A-P >= B is equivalent to\n  A >= B and P <= A-B. Precompute A-B while the reciprocal refines.\n  Register the low product bits directly from the DSP on pass 6. The next\n  cycle can compare P with A-B while forming both candidate remainders.\n\n  Fold sign restoration into those two parallel differences. For sign\n  flag n, form X + ~P + (1-n) for X equal to A and A-B. XOR the selected\n  word with a mask of n. This gives X-P for a positive result and P-X for\n  a negative result. Compute the adjacent quotient on pass 6 so DIV and\n  REM share the final XOR. All arithmetic on result words wraps at 32 bits.\n\n  The scratch implementation completed ten CoreMark iterations in\n  3,081,605 bracketed cycles with both buses stalling and all five CRCs\n  correct. Gowin placements 0, 1 and 2 reached 83.100, 87.580 and\n  87.580 MHz. The median gives 284.20 iterations/s, 4.71% above 271.43.\n  The promotion threshold is 283.92 iterations/s, so t\n…[1195 of 4267 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:3dd569b7fdff683f]…\naw_product_q + {31'b0, !negate_q}\n        r1 = a_minus_b_q[31:0] + ~raw_product_q + {31'b0, !negate_q}\n        q = (correct ^ negate_q) ? bumped_q : quotient_q\n        word = ({32{want_rem_q && !correct}} & r0) |\n               ({32{want_rem_q && correct}} & r1) | ({32{!want_rem_q}} & q)\n        div_result = !want_rem_q && zero_q ? 32'hffff_ffff : word ^ {32{negate_q}}\n\n      Use unsigned 32-bit result words and a 33-bit a_minus_b_q. At B=0\n      both remainder candidates restore the original dividend. Preserve\n      the ALTOPS formulas, the common issue/valid/ready timing and stable\n      output under backpressure.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Use magnitudes 6/3 and 5/3 to exercise P equal to A-B and P greater\n      than A-B, respectively. Check both quotient and remainder with all\n      four sign combinations. Include A<B to exercise the saved borrow\n      and a negative REM by zero with result_ready held low. Check the\n      full architectural word and the existing handshake timing.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
