{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor r in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if r['id'].endswith(('r13s0','r12s0','r13s1','r13s2','r11s0')):\n  print(r['id'],r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261121-001-r11s0 Look up the existing 512-row successor table one fetch earlier. While fetching A and predicting B, send B's nine index bits to the synchronous read port. During B the RAM presents the row for B, which contains its previously observed successor C and C's instruction. At the edge admitting B, capture this row in fabric flip-flops. During C, the saved instruction, its address and its direct-target metadata are available from those flip-flops. A warm stream still admits one instruction per clock.\n\nThe lookup is speculative and internal. Use the low bits of the sequential or predicted direct address without waiting for full target-range validation, EX redirect or the load-use interlock. Check the registered probe index against the actual B index before promoting its response. Keep the full word-address check before issuing C from that response. A bad probe costs a cache opportunity. A ready bus can still supply the instruction immediately. Stage accepted training pairs for one clock so the physical write port takes registered inputs.\n\nThe first lookahead prototype completed ten iterations in 3,107,313 bracketed cycles with all five CRCs. At that count the median must exceed 84.162 MHz for promotion. A saved instruction initially timed out across load-use and divide holds. Adding a demand re-read of the last admitted predecessor fixed that case and passed all 38 pipeline tests. The revised design still needs a bracketed CoreMark run and median timing. The main risks are missed probes after redirects and a new timing path into the nine-bit RAM address.\n\nhyp-20261121-001-r12s0 Keep the seven-pass Newton schedule and retime its final correction. Let\nA and B be the dividend and divisor magnitudes, Q the existing quotient\nestimate and P = Q*B. For B > 0 the estimate is exact or one low, so\nP fits in 32 bits. The correction test A-P >= B is equivalent to\nA >= B and P <= A-B. Precompute A-B while the reciprocal refines.\nRegister the low product bits directly from the DSP on pass 6. The next\ncycle can co\n…[5826 of 8898 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:64bd021ec76082be]…\nep two separate\n512-bit presence maps, read both by predecessor index and register their\noutputs. The taken presence bit can authorize steering independently of\nthe block RAM data. Clear both maps together in the existing 512-clock\nreset or FENCE.I sweep. Qualify a read against writes to its full\nten-bit bank and row address.\n\nPreserve the agree-counter decision, full target verification in EX and\nexact selected-PC qualification for saved instructions on waits, holds\nand redirects. An alias may supply a speculative taken target. Its word\ncan issue only for the actual address selected for that fetch.\n\nIn a scratch implementation ten iterations took 3,053,325 bracketed\ncycles with both buses stalling and all five CRCs correct, saving 28,280\ncycles. At this cycle count promotion requires over 90.77 MHz. One\nplacement reached 86.628 MHz. The remaining timing opportunity is to\nregister the training write before it fans out to payload and presence\nmemories. The forecast assumes this retiming reaches about 91 MHz.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
