{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_119","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-001-r14s0.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261121-001-r14s0\ntitle: Predecode result selection and reuse the EX address adders for ADDI and AUIPC\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion has three ways to add in EX. The integer ALU waits for its\n  PC-versus-rs1 and immediate-versus-rs2 muxes, although the address adders\n  already compute precisely the values ADDI and AUIPC need. Gowin reported\n  16.710 ns to the EX result register on the champion's median placement.\n  The resolved load tag to the MEM/WB result was only 0.002 ns longer.\nhypothesis: |\n  Decode the source of each architectural result one stage before the data\n  arrives. Select rs1+imm from the effective-address adder for legal ADDI\n  and PC+imm from the direct-target adder for AUIPC. Give register ADD and\n  SUB the two forwarded register values directly. Keep the immediate mux\n  on shift, compare and logic operands. Register the mutually exclusive\n  result enables in ID and OR the enabled words at EX/MEM alongside the\n  existing jump-link and early-load sources.\n\n  Apply the same result-selection rule at MEM/WB. On EX advance, register\n  enables for the normal EX word and for each load width and halfword lane.\n  In MEM those enables gate the selected word, half or byte directly into\n  writeback. An inactive load contributes zero, including its sign extension.\n  Keep the resolved tag check, bus handshake and raw RVFI read word intact.\n  The next EX instruction still forwards one registered WB word.\n\n  A scratch build with the EX change reached 89.492 MHz on Gowin placement\n  1, up from 87.580 MHz. Its longest path started at the resolved row tag\n  and ended at MEM/WB write data. At 3,081,605 bracketed cycles the median\n  must exceed 91.61 MHz for promotion. The remaining gain depends on moving\n  width and result decoding ahead of that late load word.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Add ID/EX result-source enables and EX/MEM writeback lane enables to the pipeline bundles.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: Decode ADDI, AUIPC and the ordinary ALU result class alongside the jump and load classes. Capture the enables with the operands.\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: Give integer ADD and SUB a direct register-operand B input. Keep the existing operand interface usable for standalone ALU tests and preserve both M-extension implementations.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Reuse mem_addr and branch_target for ADDI and AUIPC. Gate each EX result with its registered class and capture writeback lane selects from the resolved low address bits on advance.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: Use the registered classes to combine the selected load lane, ordinary EX result, product and divide result at the existing WB register. Preserve held data, trap suppression and raw RVFI memory fields.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema,pathlib\np=pathlib.Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-001-r14s0.yaml')\nh=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text());jsonschema.validate(h,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nassert h['id']==p.stem and all((p.parents[2]/v['file']).exists() for v in h['changes'])\nprint('validated',p)\nPY\ndate -u\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
