{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_102", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-001-r8s0.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261121-001-r8s0\ntitle: Capture late arithmetic results directly in the writeback register\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion takes 3,097,817 cycles for ten iterations. Gowin reports\n  a 19.674 ns path from the reciprocal ROM through the shared DSP to\n  quotient_q. Other near-critical paths start at the WB result selector,\n  pass through EX operand forwarding, and end at fetch control. At this\n  cycle count the 4.6 percent acceptance margin requires 74.887 MHz.\nhypothesis: |\n  Retime divide writeback around the existing MEM stage. Pre-scale the\n  dividend during reciprocal refinement so the quotient register takes\n  a fixed product slice. Capture the corrected divide word on its EX\n  transfer edge and forward a dependent consumer from WB. Select the\n  divide, multiply, formatted load or ordinary EX result at the input\n  to a single MEM/WB data register. Its output directly drives both WB\n  forwarding and the register file. Integer and early-hit load consumers\n  retain their EX bypass. The timed CoreMark loop performs no division.\n  \n  Pre-scaling alone reached 73.735 MHz median. A scratch implementation\n  of the full writeback change reached 74.325 MHz on placement option 1.\n  That placement is about 0.56 MHz short of the acceptance threshold.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      During pass 4, replace the consumed normalized divisor in normalized_q\n      with the dividend magnitude shifted right by k_q. Use normalized_q\n      as the multiplicand on pass 5 and latch product[65:34] directly.\n      For B > 0 the reciprocal is a lower bound with error below 2\"'^-32.\n      Discarding k dividend bits costs at most (2''^k-1)/2''^k quotient units\n      and reciprocal error costs less than 1/2''^k on the scaled dividend.\n      One residual correction remains sufficient. Keep all seven passes,\n      signed and zero-divisor semantics, MUL issue timing and ALTOPS.\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Add an is_div source bit to EX/MEM and retain one architectural write-data field in MEM/WB.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Export the valid-qualified DIV/REM classification and corrected result.\n      Latch is_div with EX/MEM. Remove the divide selection from the\n      early forwarding result. Retain operand snapshots and existing\n      division holds and bubbles.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Register the corrected divide word on div_in_ex && !div_wait &&\n      !stall_ex_mem and route it to MEM. Include div_in_ex alongside\n      mul_in_ex and unverified loads in the existing late-result interlock.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Write the MEM/WB result as four masked words ORed together. Select\n      mem_product for is_mul, the registered quotient or remainder for\n      is_div, format_load(read_word, ...) for mem_to_reg, and in.alu_result\n      when all three selects are clear. Hold the word across bus waits\n      after retirement as the forwarding network already requires.\n  - file: rtl/wb_stage.sv\n    description: Drive w_data directly from the unified result register, with existing destination and write-enable qualification.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: Exercise all 32 divisor exponents with maximal discarded low bits and dividends near exact multiples, including held responses.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Require retirement gaps of 9, 2 and 10 clocks for the existing\n      MUL-DIV-dependent-MUL-dependent-DIV sequence. A dependent store\n      with two bus waits retires four clocks after DIV. Check WB data,\n      RVFI operands, retirement order and a single accepted store.\nYAML\npython - <<'\"'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,jsonschema,yaml\nf=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-001-r8s0.yaml')\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(f.read_text()),json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Validated')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
