{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n r=json.loads(l)\n if r['id'].endswith(('r5s1','r7s2','r6s2','r8s2','r4s2')):\n  print(r['title'],r['hypothesis'].get('hypothesis'))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_32", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n r=json.loads(l)\n if r['id'].endswith(('r5s1','r7s2','r6s2','r8s2','r4s2')):\n  print(r['title'],r['hypothesis'].get('hypothesis'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Predict the successor PC and instruction with one lookup On admission of each instruction, use its PC to launch a synchronous\nlookup of its last observed successor. Each of 512 entries packs a valid\nbit, an 18-bit successor word address and the 32-bit instruction fetched\nthere. Train the preceding instruction's row when its successor enters\nID/EX with a ready bus word. This learns taken, fall-through and indirect\nedges using one read port and one write port.\n\nUse the champion's registered next PC for sequential and direct transfers.\nFor a legal JALR with a valid response, steer fetch to the predicted\ntarget while EX resolves the forwarded operand. A cold JALR starts at\nfall-through. Use the bus word whenever ready. During an imem wait,\nsupply the saved word only if its address matches the full selected PC.\nOn an address mismatch, wait for a ready bus word. A correct JALR prediction\nadmits the target on the same edge that advances the jump. If control\nflow was mispredicted, EX squashes the younger instruction and installs\nthe resolved PC even during an imem wait.\n\nAn isolated RTL prototype supplied 604,950 instructions during imem waits\nand correctly steered 12,072 of 13,735 JALRs between the CoreMark markers.\nTen iterations with both stall generators took 3,408,562 bracketed cycles,\nsaving 785,872 cycles with all five CRCs correct. Gowin reported 44.951,\n47.568 and 47.568 MHz. The median gives 139.55 iterations/s, 17.7% above\n118.57. At this cycle count 42.275 MHz clears the 4.6% acceptance margin.\nPlacement option zero used 3,039 logic cells, 623 registers and eight BSRAMs.\nThe prototype passed all 53 fast formal checks and 24 pipeline tests.\nSelftest and all three random programs matched the reference retirement\ntrace with both zero-wait and stalled buses.\n\nPipeline RV32M products through MEM and reuse the multiplier for division Give MEM a single registered-input, signed 36-by-36 multiplier. EX captures\nforwarded operands on every admitted multiply. MEM computes the product in\nparallel with the next instructio\n…[6519 of 9591 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7835a7154b518707]…\nercept, distance,\nslope and product adds at most 3*2^-20+2^-25. Thus the refined reciprocal\nunderestimates by less than 2*(2^-18+3*2^-20+2^-25)^2+2/S < 2^-32.\nDiscarding the bottom k dividend bits costs at most 1-2^-k quotient\nunits and reciprocal error on A>>k costs less than 2^-k. The prediction\nis exact or one low, so one check suffices for every nonzero divisor.\n\nAn exhaustive integer sweep of all 2^31 normalized divisors found a maximum\nreciprocal underestimate of 0.655 times 2^-32. A scratch prototype with\none shared wide multiplier ran ten CRC-validated iterations in 3,097,817\nbracketed cycles with both buses stalling. Gowin reported 68.758, 73.980\nand 73.980 MHz. That median gives 238.81 iterations/s, a 3.3% gain.\nAcceptance at this cycle count requires more than 74.887 MHz. The\nlimiting path in the shared prototype moved to fetch. Placement zero used\n3,724 logic cells, 13 BSRAMs and two DSPs. Selftest and all three random\nprograms matched the reference retirement trace with ready and stalled buses.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport shutil,os\nfrom pathlib import Path\ntmp=Path(os.environ['TMPDIR'])\nfor mode in ['match','pages','fastbase']:\n p=tmp/mode/'rtl'\n shutil.copytree('cores/bench/rtl',p)\n f=p/'core.sv'\n s=f.read_text().replace('  // Keep both the hit check', '  logic [31:0] ex_base;\\\\n  // Keep both the hit check').replace('    .mem_addr        (ex_addr),','    .mem_addr        (ex_addr),\\\\n    .base_operand    (ex_base),')\n a=s.index('  assign early_hit = ')\n b=s.index('  assign resolved_hit',a)\n if mode=='match':\n  new='''  logic [31:2] word_addr_hint;\n  logic [31:2] cin_expected;\n  logic [30:2] carry_expected;\n  logic low_carry;\n  assign word_addr_hint = {12'b0, early_row_q.tag, early_index_q};\n  assign cin_expected = ex_base[31:2] \"'^ id_ex_w.imm[31:2] ''^ word_addr_hint;\n  assign carry_expected = (ex_base[30:2] & id_ex_w.imm[30:2]) |\n                          ((ex_base[30:2] | id_ex_w.imm[30:2]) & ~word_addr_hint[30:2]);\n  assign low_carry = ex_base[1:0] > ~id_ex_w.imm[1:0];\n  assign early_hit = id_ex_w.ctrl.mem_read && early_available_q && early_row_q.valid &&\n                     naturally_aligned(id_ex_w.ctrl.mem_width, ex_addr[1:0]) &&\n                     cin_expected == {carry_expected, low_carry} &&\n                     !(update_row && write_index == early_index_q);\n'\"'''\n elif mode=='pages':\n  new='''  logic [11:0] offs;\n  logic [11:0] page_low;\n  logic [19:0] base_page, hinted_page;\n  logic m_same, m_next, m_prev;\n  assign page_low = ex_base[11:0];\n  assign offs = id_ex_w.imm[11:0];\n  assign base_page = ex_base[31:12];\n  assign hinted_page = {12'b0,early_row_q.tag};\n  assign m_same = base_page == hinted_page;\n  // Most loads do not cross 4K pages. False negatives use the resolved port.\n  assign early_hit = id_ex_w.ctrl.mem_read && early_available_q && early_row_q.valid &&\n                     naturally_aligned(i