{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_1", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md; cat schemas/hypothesis.schema.json'", "aggregated_output": "- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-001-r1s0 (regression, +21.70%): Resolving two quotient bits per stage raised median Fmax from 5.442 to 6.627 MHz, but 16 serial remainder selections still limited the EX clock even though the timed CoreMark loop executes no divides.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-002-r1s1 (improvement, +483.66%): Splitting DIV/REM across four registered passes shortened the EX timing path to eight quotient decisions per pass, and the timed CoreMark loop incurred no divider stalls because it executes neither operation.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r1s2 (regression, +11.14%): The 64-entry agree predictor and direct JAL prediction in IF saved 297,001 CoreMark cycles by avoiding one-cycle EX redirect bubbles, while the critical path through forwarding and the EX ALU still limited median Fmax to 5.648 MHz.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-001-r2s0 (improvement, +47.44%): Padding the 32-bit dividend with three leading zeros let seven uniform passes cut the divider feedback path from eight serial subtract-and-select steps to five, raising Fmax without adding divider stalls to the timed CoreMark loop.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r2s2 (regression, +6.25%): Caching targets by fetch PC cut CoreMark JALR redirects from 13,735 to 1,647 in the 128-entry BTB prototype, but shortening the four-pass divider's critical path delivered a larger throughput gain (+47.44%).\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-001-r3s0 (regression, +5.87%): Squashing via ID/EX.valid let register reads and load-use detection use the raw fetch word in parallel with EX branch resolution, raising median Fmax from 46.846 to 49.594 MHz while ten CoreMark iterations still took 4,491,485 cycles.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-002-r3s1 (regression, +8.16%): On a same-cycle instruction bus, using the resolved EX target for both io_imemAddr and the PC passed to ID and saving it for retry on stalls eliminated the taken-redirect bubble, cutting CoreMark cycles by 7.91%.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r3s2 (improvement, +13.68%): Latching the direction IF used and the alternate PC f\n…[5603 of 8675 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6b55d285b29c26d5]…\nnLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_2", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '\\\"category\\\"\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\"structural\\\"|hyp-20261121-001-r9s0' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | cut -c1-400; ls -la cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses | tail -18\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261120-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Move DIV and REM to a shared four-pass divider\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The 5.442 MHz baseline takes 4,491,485 cycles for ten CoreMark iterations.\\nGowin reports a 199.837 ns, 156-cell path through forwarding and the EX ALU.\\nThe ALU evaluates full-width signed and unsigned division and remainder\\ncombinationally. Their serial quotient \n6:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261120-002-r2s1\", \"title\": \"Fold the divider into seven five-bit passes\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"Gowin traced the champion's 36.737 ns path from quotient_q[31] to\\nremainder_q[11] inside the divider. Each clock crosses eight dependent\\nsubtract-and-select steps. The champion ran ten CoreMark iterations in\\n4,491,485 bracketed cycles at a median 31.773 MHz. The tim\n9:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261120-002-r3s1\", \"title\": \"Fetch the resolved target in the EX redirect cycle\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The champion takes 4,491,485 cycles for ten CoreMark iterations at\\n46.846 MHz. On every taken branch, JAL or JALR, EX already has the\\ntarget while IF presents the sequential PC and discards the returned\\nword. The instruction bus returns the word at the addres\n12:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261120-002-r4s1\", \"title\": \"Share one registered multiplier across all eight RV32M operations\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"Gowin placement 1 puts the champion's register-file-to-DSP-to-data-RAM\\npath at 25.402 ns and a divider feedback path at 25.399 ns. Moving\\nmultiplication to MEM alone raised the median from 49.733 to 50.165 MHz,\\nbut dependent consumers raised t\n15:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261120-002-r5s1\", \"title\": \"Pipeline RV32M products through MEM and reuse the multiplier for division\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The champion takes 3,408,562 cycles for ten iterations at 48.072 MHz.\\nGowin reports a 27.067 ns path from the register file through the EX ALU\\nto data RAM. The five-step divider feedback path reached 25.389 ns on\\nthe related load-forwa\n18:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261120-002-r6s1\", \"title\":\n…[1046 of 4118 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:386fd218d38679e4]…\nhe Newton seed ROM to the quotient\\nregister. The timed loop executes no divides, so that feedback path sets\\nthe\n26:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261121-001-r9s0\", \"title\": \"Forward a registered EX product to the next instruction\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The champion registers multiply operands in EX and produces their product in\\nMEM. An immediately dependent instruction waits a cycle for WB. On Gowin\\nplacement option 1, the shared multiplier also creates an 18.440 ns timing\\npath from the divider seed RO\n27:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261121-002-r9s1\", \"title\": \"Select physical writeback banks when decode issues each consumer\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The champion runs ten iterations in 3,097,817 cycles. Repeating Gowin\\nplacement 1 reproduced its 76.071 MHz median. The first setup path runs\\nfrom the reciprocal seed ROM through the shared DSP to MEM/WB write_data\\nin 18.440 ns. The next path s\ntotal 16\ndrwxrwx---+ 2 nobody nogroup 4096 Nov 21 01:59 .\ndrwxrwx---+ 3 nobody nogroup 4096 Nov 21 01:59 ..\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
