{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_23", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\"):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d['id'] in ('hyp-20261121-001-r8s0','hyp-20261121-001-r12s0','hyp-20261121-003-r11s2'): print(d['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "{'motivation': 'The champion takes 3,097,817 cycles for ten iterations. Gowin reports\\na 19.674 ns path from the reciprocal ROM through the shared DSP to\\nquotient_q. Other near-critical paths start at the WB result selector,\\npass through EX operand forwarding, and end at fetch control. At this\\ncycle count the 4.6 percent acceptance margin requires 74.887 MHz.\\n', 'hypothesis': 'Retime divide writeback around the existing MEM stage. Pre-scale the\\ndividend during reciprocal refinement so the quotient register takes\\na fixed product slice. Capture the corrected divide word on its EX\\ntransfer edge and forward a dependent consumer from WB. Select the\\ndivide, multiply, formatted load or ordinary EX result at the input\\nto a single MEM/WB data register. Its output directly drives both WB\\nforwarding and the register file. Integer and early-hit load consumers\\nretain their EX bypass. The timed CoreMark loop performs no division.\\n\\nPre-scaling alone reached 73.735 MHz median. A scratch implementation\\nof the full writeback change reached 74.325 MHz on placement option 1.\\nTen CRC-validated iterations with both stall generators took 3,097,817\\nbracketed cycles. This gives 239.93 iterations/s at that placement,\\nabout 0.56 MHz short of the acceptance threshold. Selftest and all\\nthree random programs matched the reference with ready and stalled buses.\\n', 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 4, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/alu.sv', 'description': 'During pass 4, replace the consumed normalized divisor in normalized_q\\nwith the dividend magnitude shifted right by k_q. Use normalized_q\\nas the multiplicand on pass 5 and latch product[65:34] directly.\\nFor B > 0 the reciprocal is a lower bound with error below 2^-32.\\nDiscarding k dividend bits costs at most (2^k-1)/2^k quotient units\\nand reciprocal error costs less than 1/2^k on the scaled dividend.\\nOne residual correction remains sufficient. Keep all seven passes,\\nsigned and zero-divisor semantics, MUL issue timing and ALTOPS.\\n'}, {'file'\n…[8990 of 12062 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:5d4a738aafb91f3a]…\n && raw_product_q <= a_minus_b_q[31:0]\\n  r0 = dividend + ~raw_product_q + {31'b0, !negate_q}\\n  r1 = a_minus_b_q[31:0] + ~raw_product_q + {31'b0, !negate_q}\\n  q = (correct ^ negate_q) ? bumped_q : quotient_q\\n  word = ({32{want_rem_q && !correct}} & r0) |\\n         ({32{want_rem_q && correct}} & r1) | ({32{!want_rem_q}} & q)\\n  div_result = !want_rem_q && zero_q ? 32'hffff_ffff : word ^ {32{negate_q}}\\n\\nUse unsigned 32-bit result words and a 33-bit a_minus_b_q. At B=0\\nboth remainder candidates restore the original dividend. Preserve\\nthe ALTOPS formulas, the common issue/valid/ready timing and stable\\noutput under backpressure.\\n\"}, {'file': 'test/test_alu.py', 'description': 'Use magnitudes 6/3 and 5/3 to exercise P equal to A-B and P greater\\nthan A-B, respectively. Check both quotient and remainder with all\\nfour sign combinations. Include A<B to exercise the saved borrow\\nand a negative REM by zero with result_ready held low. Check the\\nfull architectural word and the existing handshake timing.\\n'}]}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
