{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_138","type":"agent_message","text":"Wrote and schema-validated the [structural hypothesis](cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-002-r13s1.yaml). It proposes a one-entry posted-store buffer with byte-enabled cache updates so independent instructions and cache hits can proceed during a write stall.\n\nA prototype saved **43,227 cycles** over ten CoreMark iterations and passed all five CRC checks. Its 85.441 MHz placement fell short of the **90.323 MHz** promotion threshold. Four pipeline tests flagged changed timing or bus traffic. The proposed byte-enabled implementation still needs median Gowin timing."}}
