{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_31", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('round_id') in [10,11] and d['slot'] in [0,1]:\n  print(d['id'],d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\ndate -u\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261121-001-r10s0 Use decode's knowledge of the two physical operand sources to select\na one-bit branch outcome in EX. Compare the possible pairs of registered\nsource words in parallel. This moves both wide forwarding muxes off the\nbranch-to-fetch path and preserves single-cycle branch resolution.\nThe existing predictor supplies the predicted direction and alternate PC.\nAt the measured cycle count the median must exceed 82.95 MHz to clear\nthe acceptance margin. The main risks are routing the parallel comparisons\nand the independent saved-instruction path to the PC. The parallel-pair\ndesign has yet to be timed.\n\nhyp-20261121-002-r10s1 Make an aligned 16-byte block the unit transferred from fetch RAM to\na pair of registered instruction blocks. Decode issues one word per\ncycle from the active registers. While it consumes those words, fetch\ncan synchronously look up the following block into the other registers.\nA load interlock holds the issue cursor locally. The fetch RAM operates\nfrom registered block requests and free-slot state. On a sequential\nhit the only address update on the issue path is a two-bit slot advance.\n\nGive each slot a valid bit, the original word and predecoded direct\ncontrol-flow metadata including an eligible absolute target. Build that\nmetadata off the issue path from the word and its own PC. Retain the\ncurrent agree policy and learned JALR targets. A predicted transfer\nwithin either resident block can select its slot directly. Look up a\npredicted external block as soon as its source slot is identified.\nPass the predicted successor with the issued instruction for EX to\nverify. A correction discards younger deliveries and restarts at the\nfull resolved PC.\n\nThe bus still delivers one word per ready cycle. On a cold or partial\nblock, deliver an accepted demand word immediately and fill its slot\nindependently. A valid tag-matched slot can issue during an imem wait.\nWaiting for the entire line would penalize short basic blocks. At 3.08\nmillion cycles for ten iterations, 83.43 MHz clears the pro\n…[2753 of 5825 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:67c7bb95388c355c]…\ne\ninterlock off the RAM write port. Only aligned RAM PCs participate.\nSuppress colliding reads and clear the pending predecessor on reset\nand FENCE.I so a delayed pair cannot restore an invalidated word.\n\nEX verifies the PC actually selected for a taken transfer against its\nfull RV32IM target. A forecast on a non-taken or faulting branch can\nrecover to P+4. Preserve JALR bit-zero clearing, link suppression on\nfaults and redirect priority over an instruction wait. Aliasing may\nsteer a fetch but a saved instruction requires its full PC to match\nthe selected fetch address. Only the resolved path can retire or\nissue a store.\n\nA scratch implementation with MEM-pair training completed all ten\niterations with both buses stalling, all five canonical CRCs and\n3,083,798 bracketed cycles, a 0.69% cycle cost.\nAt that count the promotion threshold is 83.53 MHz. An 85 MHz median\nwould give 275.6 iterations/s. EX target verification and the\nsuccessor read enable are the remaining timing risks.\n\nSat Nov 21 06:07:39 UTC 2026\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
