{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_12", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nR=list(map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')))\nfor i in [38,41]:\n print(R[i]['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "{'motivation': 'An unaccepted store currently freezes every pipeline stage behind MEM,\\nincluding independent integer instructions and loads whose full word is\\nalready resident. Ten CoreMark iterations take 3,081,605 bracketed cycles.\\nRegistering a fallback lookup for unverified loads added 99,982 cycles in\\na scratch run. Ordinary stores offer a way to overlap a bus wait without\\ncharging each uncertain load an extra clock.\\n', 'hypothesis': 'Split the external write port from MEM with one posted-store entry. An\\naligned ordinary-RAM store can leave MEM once its address, byte enables\\nand replicated write data are irrevocably captured. Give a ready bus the\\nstore directly when the entry is empty. If the bus stalls, retain the\\ntransaction and let independent instructions and verified cache hits\\npass. If a second RAM store is waiting when the first is acknowledged,\\nreplace the entry on that edge. Retire each store once, in program order.\\n\\nUpdate the load buffer when MEM accepts ownership of a store. Allocate a\\nfull-word store directly. For SB or SH, probe the resolved row and merge\\nthe enabled bytes only on an exact resident tag hit with a usable read.\\nOtherwise invalidate the index. This lets a younger load observe the\\nstore while the external write waits. Keep the same-index read/write\\nveto on both probes. A demand miss or MMIO access waits its turn on the\\nexternal port. Drain older writes before allowing FENCE.I to invalidate\\nfetch and restart at PC+4, and before retirement of FENCE or EBREAK.\\n\\nImplement the store update with four byte write enables and separate\\ntag/valid storage. Write the asserted lanes directly from the store\\ndata. A hit preserves the other resident bytes in place. A partial miss\\nclears valid, so its other bytes cannot be observed. Accepted fills and\\nfull stores write all four lanes. This removes the 32-bit feedback route\\nfrom the resolved data RAM through four merge muxes back to its input.\\n\\nKeep the external address in one clocked register. When a posted write\\ncompl\n…[6981 of 10053 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:db1be1d9ad3e7d88]…\nv', 'description': 'Carry the exact predicted successor and fall-through alongside the instruction through fetch and ID/EX.'}, {'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'description': 'Latch the fetch prediction and fall-through on the same advance as their instruction and operands.'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Check the recorded prediction against the full resolved RV32IM next PC and use the matching fall-through for link writes and trap recovery.'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Connect packet admission, replay, MEM transfers and redirect recovery to the existing single-retire pipeline.'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Warm a pair that crosses a taken branch and retire it and the next pair\\nconsecutively with imemReady low. Hold each slot across a data wait\\nand replay a dependent second slot. Exercise a changed branch outcome\\nwith a wrong-path store, a head-index alias, and FENCE.I with a pending\\nresponse. Check channel-0 order, PC, instruction and memory effects.\\n'}]}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
