{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_112","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-002-r15s1.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261121-002-r15s1\ntitle: Give load-buffer misses a registered bus-service phase\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  On the champion's median Gowin placement the longest path runs from the\n  resolved load-buffer row into MEM/WB write data. The tag comparison\n  currently selects 32 bits of cache or bus data before byte extraction,\n  sign extension and writeback. Round 13 moved that selection after WB,\n  where the extra forwarding input limited EX. Ten iterations take\n  3,081,605 cycles. At that count promotion requires 91.61 MHz.\nhypothesis: |\n  Split a load's MEM service into a resident-word probe and a demand bus\n  phase. At EX/MEM capture whether this aligned load has a usable resolved\n  RAM probe. In probe mode route the RAM word to the formatter immediately.\n  The full tag and valid comparison decides only whether the slot can\n  advance. On a miss, hold the load and younger stages, suppress retirement\n  of the candidate, and set a registered bit to select the bus phase on\n  the following clock. Assert the demand read only in that phase, keep it\n  stable through waits, and fill and complete once on acceptance. Loads\n  already known to require the bus in EX, including MMIO and a probe\n  canceled by a write collision, enter the bus phase directly.\n\n  Register the load's lane and extension controls with its address. Feed\n  both phases through one formatted result into the existing MEM/WB word.\n  This removes the late RAM tag from the write-data mux while retaining\n  one WB forwarding source. A correctly predicted load still forwards\n  its verified early word to the adjacent EX consumer. A bad ID index\n  that hits at the resolved index still completes in one MEM cycle.\n  Only a usable resolved probe that actually misses pays a new clock.\n  Count those misses between the markers and compare the measured median\n  Fmax against 284.20 * 1.046 * bracketed_cycles / 10e6 MHz.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Add probe and demand phase state to the current MEM slot. Use\n      resolved_available_q on entry, latch a probe miss while the slot is\n      held, and clear the phase on reset or transfer. Drive the raw word\n      from the registered source for both formatting and RVFI. Preserve\n      reset sweep, full tag validation, early bypass and store coherence.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Hold EX/MEM and clear WB valid on a failed resident probe even if\n      dmemReady is high. Preserve held forwarding data and release the\n      demand phase only when its transaction handshakes.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Predecode byte and halfword selection and sign-extension enables\n      from the effective address and width on EX/MEM advance.\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Carry the registered load lane controls in ex_mem_t.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Apply the registered lane controls to the selected raw word. Keep\n      a single registered writeback value and generate RVFI address,\n      masks and raw data from the completing transaction.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Follow a resident hit with a same-index tag miss and a dependent\n      instruction. Withhold ready for several demand clocks, then check\n      for one accepted read, the returned subword, contiguous retirement\n      order, and a subsequent resident hit with ready low.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
