{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_122", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-002-r15s1.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261121-002-r15s1\ntitle: Gather the ALU operand and its bypass sources at issue\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion takes 3,081,605 cycles for ten iterations at 87.580 MHz.\n  On its median placement the path from a forwarded integer result back\n  to EX/MEM is within 0.002 ns of the longest load-return path. It passes\n  through register forwarding, ALU operand selection and result selection\n  in one clock. In round 14, routing ADDI around the operand mux helped,\n  but shifts, comparisons and logic operations still paid for that mux.\nhypothesis: |\n  Make the second ALU operand an explicit ID/EX pipeline value. During\n  decode gather the immediate, raw register-array word, or simultaneous\n  WB write-through into this slot with mutually exclusive enables. If a\n  younger EX or MEM writer wins, store zero and register its bypass select.\n  Enable those late sources only for register-register ALU instructions.\n  In EX, OR the gathered operand with the selected registered producer.\n  There is then no immediate-versus-register mux after forwarding. Keep\n  raw rs2 available for branches, store payloads, multiplication and RVFI.\n  Qualify array reads with the written map and give x0 zero on both paths.\n\n  Feed rs1 and this prepared operand to one adder for ADD, ADDI, load and\n  store addresses, and JALR. Give AUIPC the PC-relative target adder.\n  Register mutually exclusive operation enables in ID so integer results,\n  the link and the verified early-load candidate feed the existing EX/MEM\n  bypass register in parallel. The common adder can produce a don't-care\n  address on idle bus cycles. Store data remains independent of its\n  displacement. Keep decode legality, replay, the M-unit schedule and the\n  single channel-0 retirement boundary.\n\n  A scratch design with the prepared operand, shared adder and registered\n  result enables reproduced all five CoreMark CRCs in 3,081,605 cycles.\n  Gowin placement 1 reached 88.344 MHz. Its critical paths included a\n  fetch correction through the register file to the new operand register.\n  This motivates folding WB write-through and array eligibility into the\n  gather enables. At the observed cycle count promotion requires a median\n  above 91.610 MHz. The estimated gain assumes about 93 MHz.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/reg_file.sv\n    description: |\n      Expose raw array reads and separate written-row and same-cycle\n      WB-match indications so issue can select a physical source directly.\n      Retain the write-first interface for callers that use it.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Resolve youngest-writer priority for both register sources and the\n      prepared ALU operand. Register distinct ALU, product and WB bypass\n      enables with their consumer. Preserve the existing RF view used by\n      the speculative load-index probe.\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Add the prepared ALU operand and integer result enables to id_ex_t.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Capture the immediate, raw array word or WB write-through with\n      independent enables. Mask every early source on a late bypass match.\n      Latch the result enables from validated decode and hold all operand\n      data and selects together across a stall.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Combine the prepared operand with its qualified bypasses. Drive\n      integer execution and address generation from those values, and\n      gate each architectural result into the EX/MEM register with its\n      decoded enable. Keep multiply inputs and store data on raw rs2.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Exercise a WB write-through shadowed by a younger writer, an OP-IMM\n      whose immediate bits name a pending destination, and a store whose\n      payload and base both need forwarding. Check addresses, masks, data\n      and channel-0 order across a data-bus hold.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
