{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md && cat schemas/hypothesis.schema.json'", "aggregated_output": "- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-001-r1s0 (regression, +21.70%): Resolving two quotient bits per stage raised median Fmax from 5.442 to 6.627 MHz, but 16 serial remainder selections still limited the EX clock even though the timed CoreMark loop executes no divides.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-002-r1s1 (improvement, +483.66%): Splitting DIV/REM across four registered passes shortened the EX timing path to eight quotient decisions per pass, and the timed CoreMark loop incurred no divider stalls because it executes neither operation.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r1s2 (regression, +11.14%): The 64-entry agree predictor and direct JAL prediction in IF saved 297,001 CoreMark cycles by avoiding one-cycle EX redirect bubbles, while the critical path through forwarding and the EX ALU still limited median Fmax to 5.648 MHz.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-001-r2s0 (improvement, +47.44%): Padding the 32-bit dividend with three leading zeros let seven uniform passes cut the divider feedback path from eight serial subtract-and-select steps to five, raising Fmax without adding divider stalls to the timed CoreMark loop.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r2s2 (regression, +6.25%): Caching targets by fetch PC cut CoreMark JALR redirects from 13,735 to 1,647 in the 128-entry BTB prototype, but shortening the four-pass divider's critical path delivered a larger throughput gain (+47.44%).\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-001-r3s0 (regression, +5.87%): Squashing via ID/EX.valid let register reads and load-use detection use the raw fetch word in parallel with EX branch resolution, raising median Fmax from 46.846 to 49.594 MHz while ten CoreMark iterations still took 4,491,485 cycles.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-002-r3s1 (regression, +8.16%): On a same-cycle instruction bus, using the resolved EX target for both io_imemAddr and the PC passed to ID and saving it for retry on stalls eliminated the taken-redirect bubble, cutting CoreMark cycles by 7.91%.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r3s2 (improvement, +13.68%): Latching the direction IF used and the alternate PC f\n…[3832 of 6904 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e2ecf12947828e82]…\nnLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
