on placement option 1.\\nTen CRC-validated iterations with both stall generators took 3,097,817\\nbracketed cycles. This gives 239.93 iterations/s at that placement,\\nabout 0.56 MHz short of the acceptance threshold. Selftest and all\\nthree random programs matched the reference with ready and stalled buses.\\n', 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 4, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/alu.sv', 'description': 'During pass 4, replace the consumed \n…[5017 of 8089 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:5903b15e9a8de0ec]…\nstr_0_1_s', 'slack_ns': -8.41, 'arrival_ns': 18.653, 'logic_cells': 14, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_if']}, 'logic_levels': 12, 'formal_passed': True, 'cosim_passed': True, 'error': None, 'implementation_notes': '', 'timestamp': '2026-11-20T23:54:51.618356Z', 'slot': 0, 'round_id': 8, 'lesson': \"- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-001-r8s0 (improvement, +6.25%): Selecting the ALU, multiply, divide or formatted load result at the MEM/WB register input removed a mux from the WB-to-EX forwarding path, and waiting until WB for divide results cost no cycles in CoreMark's divide-free timed loop.\"}\nkeys dict_keys(['id', 'title', 'category', 'motivation', 'hypothesis', 'expected_impact', 'changes', 'outcome', 'fitness', 'delta_pct', 'vs_baseline', 'fmax_mhz', 'ipc_coremark', 'cycles', 'iterations', 'lut4', 'ff', 'seeds', 'perturbations', 'lutram', 'bsram', 'dsp', 'critical_path', 'logic_levels', 'formal_passed', 'cosim_passed', 'error', 'implementation_notes', 'timestamp', 'slot', 'round_id', 'lesson'])\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
