{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_116", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-002-r9s1.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261121-002-r9s1\ntitle: Select physical writeback banks when decode issues each consumer\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion runs ten iterations in 3,097,817 cycles. Repeating Gowin\n  placement 1 reproduced its 76.071 MHz median. The first setup path runs\n  from the reciprocal seed ROM through the shared DSP to MEM/WB write_data\n  in 18.440 ns. The next path starts at the registered rs1 forwarding\n  select and reaches the fetch PC in 18.438 ns. The first crosses a result\n  mux after multiplication. The second crosses a priority mux before EX\n  address generation and load-use control. Both boundaries depend on the\n  same information: which older instruction supplies an operand.\nhypothesis: |\n  Give the selected MUL word its own MEM/WB data register and retain a\n  separate bank for the ordinary result. During ID, resolve each source\n  to a physical input for its next EX cycle: the captured register-file\n  value, EX/MEM bypass, ordinary WB bank, or product WB bank. The youngest\n  matching writer and its result class are already known in ID. Capture a\n  one-hot choice with each operand and combine the four registered data\n  sources in parallel in EX. Decode the PC and immediate choices at the\n  same issue boundary so address generation and the arithmetic operand\n  ports each have a single selection network. Keep the architectural WB\n  mux at the register file and RVFI boundary, outside EX forwarding.\n\n  This preserves one multiply issue per clock, the verified early-load\n  bypass and existing dependency bubbles. A gain must come from a shorter\n  clock period. At the champion's cycle count the acceptance threshold is\n  79.57 MHz. The main risk is routing four wide sources to each operand.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Capture mem_product directly in its own word register, with an aligned\n      product-select bit. Capture ALU, formatted load or saved DIV data in\n      the ordinary bank. Hold both banks and the select through data waits.\n      Expose both data words to forwarding and select the architectural word\n      for the RF write, its write-first bypass and channel-0 retirement.\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Extend each existing youngest-writer match into four mutually exclusive\n      source enables. An older MEM-stage match selects the WB bank using that\n      producer's is_mul bit. A younger EX match has priority over both banks.\n      Use the RF source for x0 and for unmatched sources.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Capture the source enables alongside the operands on ID/EX advance.\n      Derive the arithmetic input enables from the same match and decoded\n      AUIPC and immediate controls. Preserve the unmodified source choices\n      for effective addresses, branch compares, stores and RVFI snapshots.\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Carry the raw and arithmetic operand selects in the ID/EX bundle.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Wire the producer class and both result banks to their consumers.\n      Advance source metadata on exactly the existing operand capture edge\n      and hold it through divide and memory stalls.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Use the registered enables to AND-mask and OR the physical sources at\n      each operand port. Feed rs1 directly to the existing address adder and\n      use the arithmetic-port enables for PC and immediate substitutions.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Exercise a product and an integer writer targeting the same rd in\n      both orders, plus a consumer using different banks on rs1 and rs2\n      across a data wait. Check the forwarded operands, exact result,\n      single accepted store and consecutive channel-0 retirement orders.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-002-r9s1.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text());jsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()));print(p, d['category'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
