smatch even if imemReady is low.\\nCorrect predictions admit the successor into ID/EX on the next ready slot.\\n\\nAn isolated prototype on the champion completed ten iterations in\\n4,180,499 bracketed cycles with both bus stalls enabled and all five\\nCRCs validated. This saves 310,986 cycles. Counting accepted EX\\ntransfers between the markers, the BTB reduced conditional-branch\\ncorrections from 294,425 to 42,359, JAL corrections from 49,367 to\\n1,849, and JALR corrections from 13,735 to 1,647, relative to\\nseque\n…[21080 of 24152 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a4500928872e0153]…\nerand. Issue\\nonly divides to the existing shared arithmetic unit in this core.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Split each ID-stage match against the EX writer into ordinary-result\\nand multiply-result selects using mul_in_ex. Register those selects\\nwith the operands, preserving youngest-writer priority and x0 handling.\\nFor each source, qualify the ordinary EX select with !mul_in_ex and\\nqualify the product select with mul_in_ex. Reuse the MEM match for WB.\\nRemove mul_in_ex from the late-result interlock. Keep unverified loads\\nand completed divides on their existing WB forwarding schedule.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Require consecutive retirements for an unstalled MUL-to-ALU or\\nMUL-to-MUL dependency. Exercise both source positions, signed and mixed\\nhigh words, a younger multiply overwriting an older destination, and\\na dependent store held under backpressure. Check exact RVFI operands,\\nresults, order and one accepted store. Preserve DIV-to-use interlocks.\\n'}]}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
