gister these flags and the bank choice alongside\n  the low base hint and alignment information.\n\n  For a same-page prediction the returned RAM tag identifies the required\n  base page. Verify the actual rs1 against {12'b0, selected_tag, saved_b}\n  in EX. Compare the physical operand sources in parallel and qualify the\n  results with the existing forwarding selects. This checks all 32 bits\n  and removes the resolved address adder from the early-hit decision.\n  A cross-page displacement, wrong base, unavailable bank or collision\n  uses the existing interlock and the independent resolved-address probe\n  in MEM. At 3,057,579 cycles promotion requires more than 82.815 MHz.\n  The main timing risks are routing the two RAM responses and the\n  independent fetch-PC path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Partition rows by word-index bit 4 (byte-address bit 6), maintaining\n      the total capacity and eight-bit page tags. Launch one ID read per\n      bank with the indices above. Give the writer priority in its own bank.\n      On the ID enable capture both carry flags, bank availability, lane\n      alignment, the predicted word index and the base hint. Hold the\n      metadata and responses through an ID hold. Qualify the selected row\n      with validity, page and base checks, and veto an intervening write\n      to the same word on the advancing edge. Keep the synchronous EX\n      probe of the actual word address and register its bank on the EX/MEM\n      enable. Preserve sweep invalidation, alignment, RAM bounds, partial\n      store invalidation, collision handling and MMIO routing.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Compare the expected base supplied by the predictor against the\n      captured RF operand, EX/MEM result, registered product and WB word.\n      Select the equality bit with the registered youngest-writer choice.\n      Use it only to certify the early bypass. Keep the exact effective\n      address and formatted data paths for the memory operation and RVFI.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Update buffered_xor_miss to require a bubble on the cold access and\n      consecutive retirement on the second, hot 68+4 access. Keep every\n      data, bus and order assertion. Exercise both carries at bit 6,\n      positive and negative page crossings, a wrong pointer with the same\n      low 12 bits, and byte/halfword alignment. Contrast a simultaneous\n      write to the other bank with a same-row write, including a held\n      store. Check exact forwarded values and demand-read counts.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-003-r11s2.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert d['id']==p.stem and d['category']=='predictor'\nprint(p,d['title'])\nPY\ntail -1 \\\"\"'$TMPDIR/banked-page/coremark.log\"'", "aggregated_output": "cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-003-r11s2.yaml Probe both carry outcomes of a predicted load address\n{\"ebreak\":true,\"maxcycles_hit\":false,\"oob\":false,\"bench_start_cycle\":11649,\"bench_stop_cycle\":3069228,\"bench_bracketed\":true,\"uart\":\"2K performance run parameters for coremark.\\nCoreMark Size    : 666\\nTotal ticks      : 0\\nTotal time (secs): 10\\nIterations/Sec   : 1\\nIterations       : 10\\nCompiler version : riscv32-elf-gcc\\nCompiler flags   : -O2 -march=rv32im\\nMemory location  : STACK\\nseedcrc          : 0xe9f5\\n[0]crclist       : 0xe714\\n[0]crcmatrix     : 0x1fd7\\n[0]crcstate      : 0x8e3a\\n[0]crcfinal      : 0xfcaf\\nCorrect operation validated. See README.md for run and reporting rules.\\n\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
