{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_54", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '70,110p;163,260p' test/cosim/main.cpp && head -45 test/cosim/main.cpp && ls \\\"\"'$TMPDIR/r13pred/v1/obj\" | head -15 && ls -l \"$TMPDIR/r13pred/bankmeta/obj/cosim_sim\"'", "aggregated_output": "    //           (tools/eval/fpga.py:run_coremark_ipc) passes BOTH so the\n    //           CoreMark/MHz number we score against matches VexRiscv's\n    //           published methodology rather than a zero-wait fantasy bus.\n    bool bench_mode = false;\n    bool istall = false;\n    bool dstall = false;\n    for (int i = 1; i < argc; i++) {\n        if      (std::strcmp(argv[i], \"--bench\")  == 0) bench_mode = true;\n        else if (std::strcmp(argv[i], \"--istall\") == 0) istall     = true;\n        else if (std::strcmp(argv[i], \"--dstall\") == 0) dstall     = true;\n        else if (std::strcmp(argv[i], \"--seed\")   == 0 && i + 1 < argc)\n            lfsr_state_main = (uint32_t)atoll(argv[++i]);\n    }\n\n    ELF elf; elf.load(argv[1]);\n    for(int i=0;i<elf.phnum();i++){\n        uint32_t off    = elf.phoff() + i*elf.phentsize();\n        uint32_t type   = *reinterpret_cast<uint32_t*>(&elf.data[off]);\n        uint32_t foff   = *reinterpret_cast<uint32_t*>(&elf.data[off+4]);\n        uint32_t vaddr  = *reinterpret_cast<uint32_t*>(&elf.data[off+8]);\n        uint32_t filesz = *reinterpret_cast<uint32_t*>(&elf.data[off+16]);\n        if(type==1 && vaddr < (1<<20)) {\n            memcpy(imem+vaddr, elf.data.data()+foff, filesz);\n            memcpy(dmem+vaddr, elf.data.data()+foff, filesz);\n        }\n    }\n\n    Verilated::commandArgs(argc, argv);\n    Vcore* top = new Vcore;\n    top->reset = 1; top->clock = 0;\n    top->io_imemReady = 1;\n    top->io_dmemReady = 1;\n    for(int i=0;i<5;i++){top->clock=0;top->eval();top->clock=1;top->eval();}\n    top->reset = 0;\n\n    char bench_last[512] = {};\n    bool hit_ebreak = false;\n    // UART capture: writes to 0x10000000 go to stdout as characters, not dmem.\n    // CoreMark's portme.c redirects ee_printf through this MMIO so the bench\n    // driver can parse \"CoreMark Size\"/\"ERROR!\" banners for CRC validation.\n    std::string uart_buf;\n                for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) {\n                    if ((top->io_dmemWEn >> i) & 1) {\n                        char c = (top->io_dmemWData >> (i * 8)) & \n…[5893 of 8965 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6095d2589b59757b]…\nnchmark-time MMIO markers. CoreMark's portme.c writes to BENCH_START\n// from start_time() and BENCH_STOP from stop_time(); the sim records the\n// cycle count at each write so run_fpga_eval can compute\n// bench_cycles = stop - start, excluding init/CRC-printing overhead.\nstatic constexpr uint32_t BENCH_START_ADDR = 0x10000100u;\nstatic constexpr uint32_t BENCH_STOP_ADDR  = 0x10000104u;\n\nuint32_t rw(uint8_t* m, uint32_t a) {\n    a &= 0xFFFFC;\n    return m[a]|(m[a+1]<<8)|(m[a+2]<<16)|(m[a+3]<<24);\n}\nvoid ww(uint8_t* m, uint32_t a, uint32_t v, uint8_t mask) {\n    a &= 0xFFFFC;\n    for(int i=0;i<4;i++) if((mask>>i)&1) m[a+i]=(v>>(i*8))&0xFF;\nVcore.cpp\nVcore.h\nVcore.mk\nVcore__ALL.a\nVcore__ALL.cpp\nVcore__ALL.d\nVcore__ALL.o\nVcore__ConstPool__0__Slow.cpp\nVcore__Syms.h\nVcore__Syms__Slow.cpp\nVcore___024root.h\nVcore___024root__0.cpp\nVcore___024root__0__Slow.cpp\nVcore___024root__Slow.cpp\nVcore___024unit.h\n-rwxrwx---+ 1 hwebench hwebench 248448 Nov 21 05:56 /srv/hwebench/tmp/ec844b20/ebae9a88/r13pred/bankmeta/obj/cosim_sim\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_55","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nd=[json.loads(l) for l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')];print(next(i['hypothesis']['hypothesis'] for i in d if i['id'].endswith('r1s2')))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_55","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nd=[json.loads(l) for l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')];print(next(i['hypothesis']['hypothesis'] for i in d if i['id'].endswith('r1s2')))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"Index 64 two-bit saturating counters with fetch PC[7:2]. Use the offset\nsign as the default direction for a legal conditional branch (backward\ntaken, forward fall-through). Predict taken = offset_sign XOR counter[1].\nThe counter learns whether to invert the default, so a hot backedge and\na usually untaken forward guard can share an entry constructively. Predict\ndirect JAL taken. Compute the signed B/J target in parallel with the table\nlookup and select it only for a word-aligned address in instruction RAM.\nUse PC+4 for every other fetch, including JALR. Carry the selected direction\nbit with the accepted instruction. Direct targets are exact by construction,\nso EX can detect a miss by comparing this bit with the resolved direction.\nA miss redirects to the resolved next PC and kills the younger instruction.\nCorrect predictions let the successor enter ID/EX immediately. An isolated\nRTL prototype completed ten 2K CoreMark iterations in 4,194,484 bracketed\ncycles with both bus stalls enabled, versus 4,491,485 on the baseline.\nAll five CRCs matched. Gowin reported 5.214, 5.486 and 5.486 MHz across\nthe three placement options. The median gives 13.08 iter/s, a 7.9% gain\nover 12.12. The prototype used 12 LUT-RAM primitives versus 8 at baseline.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
