{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_108","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-003-r13s2.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261121-003-r13s2\ntitle: Keep a separate successor word for each predicted branch outcome\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  A fall-through iteration overwrites a branch's learned taken target in\n  the champion's successor RAM. A later correct taken-direction forecast\n  can therefore fetch PC+4 and require an EX redirect. The overwrite also\n  loses the target instruction that could have satisfied an instruction-bus\n  wait. On the timed trace, enlarging the agree table from 64 to 256 entries\n  removes only 6,716 direction misses across 529,588 conditional branches.\nhypothesis: |\n  Give each predecessor index two successor rows, one for P+4 and one for\n  a nonsequential edge. Feed the current legal JAL, legal JALR or predicted\n  taken conditional request into the high bit of a synchronous 1024-row\n  lookup. The other nine address bits are P[10:2]. Both rows carry the\n  observed successor's 18-bit word address and 32-bit instruction. A loop\n  exit updates the fall-through row while the backedge target stays warm.\n\n  Train on consecutive valid MEM transfers. Capture (P+4)[19:2] with the\n  predecessor index, then classify the next transferred PC against it.\n  Accept pairs only within aligned instruction RAM. Keep two separate\n  512-bit presence maps, read both by predecessor index and register their\n  outputs. The taken presence bit can authorize steering independently of\n  the block RAM data. Clear both maps together in the existing 512-clock\n  reset or FENCE.I sweep. Qualify a read against writes to its full\n  ten-bit bank and row address.\n\n  Preserve the agree-counter decision, full target verification in EX and\n  exact selected-PC qualification for saved instructions on waits, holds\n  and redirects. An alias may supply a speculative taken target. Its word\n  can issue only for the actual address selected for that fetch.\n\n  In a scratch implementation ten iterations took 3,053,325 bracketed\n  cycles with both buses stalling and all five CRCs correct, saving 28,280\n  cycles. At this cycle count promotion requires over 90.77 MHz. One\n  placement reached 86.628 MHz. The remaining timing opportunity is to\n  register the training write before it fans out to payload and presence\n  memories. The forecast assumes this retiming reaches about 91 MHz.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Key the successor payload by {requested_nonsequential, pc[10:2]}.\n      Register its bank choice and the two presence bits with the read.\n      Stage the observed successor PC, word, bank, predecessor index and\n      write enable together after MEM transfer. Qualify read/write\n      collisions against that physical write and invalidate pending\n      training on reset or FENCE.I. Keep bus priority and preserve the\n      selected PC, word and forecast across holds and replays.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Warm both outcomes of one branch using distinct successor words.\n      Withhold imemReady on each revisit and check that both learned words\n      can issue, including the first taken recurrence after an exit. Cover\n      a same-bank index alias, concurrent fill, held MEM transfer and\n      FENCE.I with a pending fill. Check channel-0 PCs, raw instructions,\n      order and wrong-path store suppression.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\nd=yaml.safe_load(open('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-003-r13s2.yaml'))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint(d['title'],284.20*1.046*3053325/10000000)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
