clock edge. Hold it on stall_id alongside\\nthe existing selects and propagate it to EX. Honor x0 and the\\nexisting load and divide availability interlocks.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Compare nine distinct physical pairs directly. These are RF1/RF2,\\nRF1 against each of ordinary, product and WB, each of those three\\nagainst RF2, and ordinary/WB and product/WB. Ordinary and product\\nare alternatives for a single EX writer, so they cannot supply\\ndifferent sources on the same issue. Two operands selecting the same\\n\n…[26963 of 30035 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:d8aa0c0631dea0e1]…\nnd\\nwrite enable together after MEM transfer. Qualify read/write\\ncollisions against that physical write and invalidate pending\\ntraining on reset or FENCE.I. Keep bus priority and preserve the\\nselected PC, word and forecast across holds and replays.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Warm both outcomes of one branch using distinct successor words.\\nWithhold imemReady on each revisit and check that both learned words\\ncan issue, including the first taken recurrence after an exit. Cover\\na same-bank index alias, concurrent fill, held MEM transfer and\\nFENCE.I with a pending fill. Check channel-0 PCs, raw instructions,\\norder and wrong-path store suppression.\\n'}]\ncritical_path {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_1_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_29_s0', 'slack_ns': -6.542, 'arrival_ns': 16.836, 'logic_cells': 38, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nseeds [86.64, 87.915, 87.915]\nperturbations [[0, 86.64, 14], [1, 87.915, 11], [2, 87.915, 11]]\nbsram 15\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
