{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_12", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor r in list(map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')))[-10:]:\n print(r['id'],r['motivation'][:1150],r['seeds'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261121-003-r10s2 On the champion's 79.301 MHz placement, four of the five longest setup\npaths run from the saved successor instruction into the fetch PC. The\nworst goes through offset selection, carry propagation and the RAM-range\ncheck before driving PC bit 30. A replay of 529,588 conditional branches\nfrom the timed trace found that expanding the agree predictor from 64 to\n256 counters would remove only 6,716 direction misses. At one bubble per\nmiss that is about 0.22% of the champion's 3,062,533 cycles.\n [76.702, 80.074, 80.074]\nhyp-20261121-001-r11s0 Four of the five longest paths on the champion's 79.301 MHz placement ran from the successor RAM to the fetch PC. The split-target experiment reached 80.074 MHz and put EX forwarding and address generation on the path to the RAM write enable. A scratch implementation that queued the writes and stored an absolute direct target preserved all five CRCs and 3,062,533 bracketed cycles, but reached only 76.294 MHz on placement 1. A register between the RAM output and fetch steering could shorten the read path while keeping training writes off the admission path.\n [80.589, 81.435, 81.435]\nhyp-20261121-002-r11s1 The champion takes 3,062,533 cycles for ten iterations at 79.301 MHz.\nOn its median placement the saved instruction passes through displacement\ndecoding, a target adder and a range check on a 17.904 ns path back to\nthe PC. The path from EX forwarding to the successor RAM is 17.807 ns.\nThe four-word fetch prototype added 44,559 cycles. The existing one-word\nRAM already delivers an aligned successor address in time to steer JALR.\n [79.549, 83.645, 83.645]\nhyp-20261121-003-r11s2 The early load predictor uses XOR for the word index. A base of 68 and\ndisplacement of 4 therefore probe the resident word at 64 even though\nthe consumer needs 72. EX then puts forwarded rs1, a full-width address\naddition and a hit check on the path to fetch admission. A scratch\npredictor with a full-width base hint and one address adder saved\n4,954 cycles, but Gowin placement 1 reached\n…[1930 of 5002 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4746cc78824b6f38]…\nle count,\npromotion requires a median above 91.61 MHz.\n [80.891, 86.589, 86.589]\nhyp-20261121-002-r13s1 An unaccepted store currently freezes every pipeline stage behind MEM,\nincluding independent integer instructions and loads whose full word is\nalready resident. Ten CoreMark iterations take 3,081,605 bracketed cycles.\nRegistering a fallback lookup for unverified loads added 99,982 cycles in\na scratch run. Ordinary stores offer a way to overlap a bus wait without\ncharging each uncertain load an extra clock.\n [81.065, 84.511, 84.511]\nhyp-20261121-003-r13s2 A fall-through iteration overwrites a branch's learned taken target in\nthe champion's successor RAM. A later correct taken-direction forecast\ncan therefore fetch PC+4 and require an EX redirect. The overwrite also\nloses the target instruction that could have satisfied an instruction-bus\nwait. On the timed trace, enlarging the agree table from 64 to 256 entries\nremoves only 6,716 direction misses across 529,588 conditional branches.\n [86.64, 87.915, 87.915]\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
