{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor r in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if r['id'].endswith('r11s0'):\n  print(r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'],r['changes'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_20", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor r in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if r['id'].endswith('r11s0'):\n  print(r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'],r['changes'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Look up the existing 512-row successor table one fetch earlier. While fetching A and predicting B, send B's nine index bits to the synchronous read port. During B the RAM presents the row for B, which contains its previously observed successor C and C's instruction. At the edge admitting B, capture this row in fabric flip-flops. During C, the saved instruction, its address and its direct-target metadata are available from those flip-flops. A warm stream still admits one instruction per clock.\n\nThe lookup is speculative and internal. Use the low bits of the sequential or predicted direct address without waiting for full target-range validation, EX redirect or the load-use interlock. Check the registered probe index against the actual B index before promoting its response. Keep the full word-address check before issuing C from that response. A bad probe costs a cache opportunity. A ready bus can still supply the instruction immediately. Stage accepted training pairs for one clock so the physical write port takes registered inputs.\n\nThe first lookahead prototype completed ten iterations in 3,107,313 bracketed cycles with all five CRCs. At that count the median must exceed 84.162 MHz for promotion. A saved instruction initially timed out across load-use and divide holds. Adding a demand re-read of the last admitted predecessor fixed that case and passed all 38 pipeline tests. The revised design still needs a bracketed CoreMark run and median timing. The main risks are missed probes after redirects and a new timing path into the nine-bit RAM address.\n [{'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'description': \"Retain the successor-table indexing and agree counters. Give the read port a free-running lookahead index. Carry the sampled index and collision validity with its output. Promote a matching row only for an admitted RAM PC. Preserve a usable response across holds, and if a missing saved word blocks fetch, re-read the last admitted predecessor index, even while admission is stalled. Install its response independently of admission only on a full match to the waiting PC. Cancel that demand response on redirect, invalidation or collision. The last admitted predecessor must survive a redirect so the resolved entry can be trained. Keep the admitted successor word stable across repeated waits. A ready bus word overrides cached data and drives its own B/J prediction. Train from a registered predecessor index, successor PC, bus word and enable. Use the write stage to pack the successor instruction's aligned in-RAM B/J target and eligibility bits. Verify legal JALR steering in EX. Invalidate or forward reads that conflict with a pending or intervening write, including a held probe. Preserve the existing logical same-row collision veto. On reset or an admitted FENCE.I discard pending fills, probes and held responses and let the sweep take priority.\\n\"}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': \"On a direct direction miss, form the recovery PC from the issuing instruction's registered PC and immediate. Choose PC+4 for a predicted-taken miss and the full target for a predicted-fallthrough miss. This lets IF store only the aligned RAM target in a row. Keep the advancing-instruction qualification, JALR target comparison, trap handling and channel-0 retirement behavior.\\n\"}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Exercise a warm direct-branch loop with the instruction bus held low, a redirect whose correct target has a different probe index, and a held probe overwritten before promotion. Cross a 512-row alias and admit FENCE.I with a queued fill. Check fetch recovery, exact channel-0 instructions, PCs, order and store effects, plus consecutive retirements on a warmed correct lookahead.\\n'}]\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
