{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_94","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'tail -4 \"$TMPDIR/rawtarget1/gw.log\" && tail -4 \"$TMPDIR/rawpcq1/gw.log\" && sed -n '\"'1,140p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-003-r14s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"Running placement......\n[10%] Placement Phase 0 completed\n[20%] Placement Phase 1 completed\n[30%] Placement Phase 2 completed\nRunning placement......\n[10%] Placement Phase 0 completed\n[20%] Placement Phase 1 completed\n[30%] Placement Phase 2 completed\nid: hyp-20261121-003-r14s2\ntitle: Carry the next sequential address in each successor prediction\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  In r12s1 and r12s2, Gowin placement 0 traced the worst path from the\n  successor RAM to the upper bits of fallthrough_q. A predicted target\n  passes through fetch-PC selection before IF can increment it for the\n  following cycle. The two-outcome predictor in r13s2 saved only 26,223\n  of 3,081,605 cycles. Timing offers more leverage on this core.\nhypothesis: |\n  Train each successor row with both the observed target T and the exact\n  address T+4. On a predicted transfer the row can then deliver the next\n  instruction, its PC and its fall-through together. Move the other\n  increments to their respective PC sources as well. This removes the\n  carry chain following the fetch selector without adding a fetch stage\n  or changing the 64-counter direction policy. At the champion cycle\n  count, promotion requires a median above 91.61 MHz. About 93 MHz would\n  yield 302 iterations/s. The competing EX ALU and load-buffer paths make\n  that clock gain uncertain.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      During MEM-pair training, form T+4 from the aligned successor PC.\n      Keep the carry into bit 20 for a target at the last RAM word.\n      Select the next fallthrough_q from the same mutually exclusive\n      sources as the fetch PC. Use 4 on reset, resolved_pc+4 on recovery,\n      the saved PC's companion on hold or replay, the row companion when\n      steering, and fallthrough_q+4 on a sequential advance. Capture the\n      held companion alongside held_pc_q on every edge and update the EX\n      fall-through only on !stall_id. Keep the row read synchronous, the\n      training write qualified by MEM transfer, and the existing collision,\n      FENCE.I, sweep and full-address checks for reusing an instruction.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Exercise a warmed taken target immediately followed by a JAL and\n      verify its link. Place targets just below a carry boundary. Check\n      channel-0 PCs and link values through repeated instruction waits,\n      a data stall, a load-use replay, a wrong-target redirect and FENCE.I.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
