{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor row in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n print(row['id'],row['cycles'],row['fmax_mhz'],row['bsram'],row['category'])\n if row['id'].endswith(('r7s2','r7s0','r4s2','r7s1','r6s2')): print(row['hypothesis'].get('hypothesis',''),str(row.get('critical_path'))[:3200])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "baseline-bench-4f20506 4491485 5.442 6 micro_opt\nhyp-20261120-001-r1s0 4491485 6.627 6 micro_opt\nhyp-20261120-002-r1s1 4491485 31.773 6 structural\nhyp-20261120-003-r1s2 4194484 5.648 6 predictor\nhyp-20261120-001-r2s0 4491485 46.846 6 micro_opt\nhyp-20261120-002-r2s1 4491485 46.846 6 structural\nhyp-20261120-003-r2s2 4180499 31.421 7 predictor\nhyp-20261120-001-r3s0 4491485 49.594 6 micro_opt\nhyp-20261120-002-r3s1 4136096 46.659 6 structural\nhyp-20261120-003-r3s2 4194434 49.733 6 predictor\nhyp-20261120-001-r4s0 3990037 50.844 6 micro_opt\nhyp-20261120-002-r4s1 4382865 61.695 7 structural\nhyp-20261120-003-r4s2 3408562 48.072 8 predictor\nOn admission of each instruction, use its PC to launch a synchronous\nlookup of its last observed successor. Each of 512 entries packs a valid\nbit, an 18-bit successor word address and the 32-bit instruction fetched\nthere. Train the preceding instruction's row when its successor enters\nID/EX with a ready bus word. This learns taken, fall-through and indirect\nedges using one read port and one write port.\n\nUse the champion's registered next PC for sequential and direct transfers.\nFor a legal JALR with a valid response, steer fetch to the predicted\ntarget while EX resolves the forwarded operand. A cold JALR starts at\nfall-through. Use the bus word whenever ready. During an imem wait,\nsupply the saved word only if its address matches the full selected PC.\nOn an address mismatch, wait for a ready bus word. A correct JALR prediction\nadmits the target on the same edge that advances the jump. If control\nflow was mispredicted, EX squashes the younger instruction and installs\nthe resolved PC even during an imem wait.\n\nAn isolated RTL prototype supplied 604,950 instructions during imem waits\nand correctly steered 12,072 of 13,735 JALRs between the CoreMark markers.\nTen iterations with both stall generators took 3,408,562 bracketed cycles,\nsaving 785,872 cycles with all five CRCs correct. Gowin reported 44.951,\n47.568 and 47.568 MHz. The median gives 139.55 iterations/s, 17.7% above\n118.57. At this \n…[9287 of 12359 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:9603f9e349b54284]…\n817, saving 198,158 cycles against that control\nand 346,402 against the champion. Between the MMIO markers, 198,068 of\n203,870 immediate load dependencies observed by the interlock had an\nearly hit. The resolved lookup served 528,626 of 544,852 loads. Both\nbus stalls were enabled and all five CRCs matched.\n\nThe scratch build reached 67.387, 69.700 and 69.700 MHz in Gowin. The\nmedian gives 225.0 iterations/s, 9.0% above 206.41. At this cycle count\nthe 4.6% acceptance margin requires more than 66.8834 MHz. Placement\noption zero used 3,675 logic cells and 13 BSRAMs, versus 3,306 and\nseven on the champion. The prototype passed all 53 fast formal checks\nand 32 pipeline tests, including two directed warm-buffer tests. Selftest\nand the three random programs matched the reference retirement trace\nwith zero-wait and stalled buses.\n {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/seed_seed_0_0_s', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_8_s0', 'slack_ns': -9.379, 'arrival_ns': 19.674, 'logic_cells': 10, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
