{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_13", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor row in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if row['id'].endswith(('r5s1','r4s1','r2s0','r6s1','r3s2','r5s0','r5s2')):print(row['id'],row['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261120-001-r2s0 {'motivation': \"The 31.773 MHz champion's reported 36.737 ns worst path runs from quotient_q[31]\\nto remainder_q[11] through eight dependent subtract-and-select steps. The timed\\nCoreMark loop executes no DIV or REM, so spending three more clocks on those\\ninstructions can buy clock frequency for every instruction in the loop.\\n\", 'hypothesis': \"Retune the existing blocking divider to compute five binary quotient bits per\\nclock over seven passes. Feed it three leading zero dividend bits so every pass\\nuses the same five-step datapath. This removes three serial carry chains and\\ntheir remainder muxes from the feedback path. Seven compute clocks also leave\\nroom for issue, transfer and a redirect or load-use bubble within the formal\\nwrapper's ten-cycle forward-progress window.\\n\\nExpect close to the champion's 4,491,485 bracketed cycles for ten iterations.\\nSetup divides can shift the stall generator's phase. At that cycle count a\\nmedian Fmax above 33.24 MHz clears the acceptance margin. A 25% gain would\\nrequire about 39.72 MHz. The single-cycle multiply path may cap the gain.\\n\", 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 25, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/alu.sv', 'description': 'Load the shared dividend/quotient shift register with the 32-bit magnitude\\nzero-extended to 35 bits. Each of five restoring steps consumes its MSB,\\nsubtracts the divisor from the shifted remainder, selects by borrow and\\nappends one quotient bit. Use a three-bit pass counter and assert result\\nvalid after pass index six. Select the low 32 quotient bits or the final\\n32-bit remainder and apply the existing sign correction. This also yields\\nall ones in the low quotient for a zero divisor. Use the same seven-pass\\ncontroller for the issue-sampled ALTOPS result and hold either result\\nuntil acknowledged.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_alu.py', 'description': 'Check request-ready and result-valid on each of the seven compute clocks,\\nthen check result stability through backpressure. Exercise the padded\n…[28646 of 31718 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:771614e862a556fa]…\nission after control-transfer trap\\nchecks. For each source, mask the three candidate values with\\nthe registered selector and OR them into the operand used for all\\nEX operations, store data and the RVFI source snapshot.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/mem_stage.sv', 'description': \"Expose the write permission after the memory alignment check for\\nID's older-producer match. Preserve the MEM/WB forwarding payload\\nwhen a data-bus wait clears its retirement valid bit.\\n\"}, {'file': 'test/test_reg_file.py', 'description': 'Write distinct nonzero words to x5 and x21, reset again, and\\ncheck both read ports return zero. Write x21 and check x5 still\\nreads zero.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Check that both sources select the younger of two writers to x5.\\nFollow a misaligned load and a misaligned JALR with consumers of\\ntheir suppressed destinations. Hold a consumer behind a waiting\\nload while its other source retires. Check source values, order,\\ntraps and the single accepted dependent store.\\n'}]}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
